("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "The name 	‘Romania’ didn’t refer to Wallachia or Moldavia until 1859, and Transylvania remained part of the Astro-Hungarian empire until 1918. Yet, throughout its marked history, the people that reside in the region we call ‘Romania’ today are united by a common history of rising up to defend themselves."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "直到1859年，'罗马尼亚'这个名字才指瓦拉几亚或摩尔达维亚，而特兰西瓦尼亚直到1918年仍是奥匈帝国的一部分。然而，在其显著的历史中，居住在我们今天称为'罗马尼亚'的地区的人们因共同的历史而团结起来，奋起保卫自己。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "During the Antiquity Period, ancient Romania was inhabited by Thracian tribes. The Greeks called them the Getae, the Romans called them Dacians, but they were a single Geto-Dacian people.  From the 7th century BCE, the Greeks established trading colonies along the Black Sea at Callatis (Mangalia), Tomis (Constanţa) and Histria. In the 1st century BC, a strong Dacian state was established by King Burebista to counter the Roman threat. The last Dacian king, Decebal (r AD 87–106), consolidated this state but was unable to stave off attacks led by the Roman emperor Trajan in 101–2. Further attacks ensued in 105–6, leading to the Roman victory at the Dacian capital of Sarmizegetusa and the final Roman conquest of the region. Dacia thus became a province of the Roman Empire."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "在古典时期，古罗马尼亚是由色雷斯部落居住的。希腊人称他们为盖塔人，罗马人称他们为达契亚人，但他们是单一的盖塔-达契亚民族。 从公元前7世纪开始，希腊人在黑海沿岸的卡拉提斯（曼加里亚）、托米斯（康斯坦察）和希斯特里亚建立了贸易殖民地。公元前1世纪，布列比斯塔国王建立了一个强大的达契亚国家，以对抗罗马的威胁。最后一位达契亚国王德塞巴尔（Decebal，公元87-106年）巩固了这个国家，但未能抵挡罗马皇帝图拉真在101-2年的攻击。随后在105-6年又发生了进一步的攻击，导致罗马人在达契亚首都萨米兹盖图萨取得胜利，并最终征服了该地区。达契亚因此成为罗马帝国的一个行省。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "The Romans recorded their expansion north of the Danube on two famous monuments: Trajan’s Column in Rome, and the ‘Tropaeum Trajani’ at Adamclisi, on the site of their victory in Dobrogea. Most of present Romania, including the Transylvanian plateau, came under their rule. The slave-owning Romans brought with them a superior civilisation and mixed with the conquered tribes to form a Daco-Roman people speaking Latin. Faced with Goth attacks in AD 271, Emperor Aurelian (r 270–75) decided to withdraw the Roman legions south of the Danube after Rome had governed the region for just under 175 years."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "罗马人将他们在多瑙河以北的扩张记录在两个著名的纪念碑上。罗马的图拉真柱，以及位于阿达姆克里西的'图拉真胜利纪念碑'，位于他们在多布罗加的胜利之地。目前罗马尼亚的大部分地区，包括特兰西瓦尼亚高原，都在他们的统治之下。拥有奴隶制的罗马人带来了优越的文明，并与被征服的部落混合，形成了一个讲拉丁语的达契亚-罗马人。公元271年，面对哥特人的攻击，奥勒良皇帝（R 270-75）决定将罗马军团撤回多瑙河以南，此前罗马已经统治该地区不到175年。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "By the Middle Ages, waves of migrating peoples, including the Goths, Huns, Avars, Slavs, Bulgars and Magyars (Hungarians), swept across this territory, each leaving their mark on the local culture, language and gene pool. Romanians survived in village communities and gradually assimilated the Slavs and other peoples who settled there, but by the 10th century, a fragmented feudal system ruled by a military class appeared."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "到了中世纪，一波又一波的移民，包括哥特人、匈奴人、阿瓦尔人、斯拉夫人、保加利亚人和马札尔人（匈牙利人），席卷了这片领土，每个民族都在当地文化、语言和基因库中留下了自己的印记。罗马尼亚人在乡村社区生存下来，并逐渐同化了定居在那里的斯拉夫人和其他民族，但到了10世纪，出现了一个由军事阶层统治的零散的封建制度。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "From the 10th century the Magyars expanded into Transylvania, north and west of the Carpathian Mountains, and by the 13th century all of Transylvania was an autonomous principality under the Hungarian crown. Following devastating Tartar raids on Transylvania in 1241 and 1242, King Bela IV of Hungary persuaded German Saxons to settle in Transylvania with free land and tax incentives. He wanted to defend the crown’s southeastern flank. He also granted the Székelys – a Hungarian ethnic group who had earlier migrated to the region with the Magyars – autonomy in return for their military support."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "从10世纪开始，马札尔人扩张到特兰西瓦尼亚，在喀尔巴阡山脉以北和以西，到13世纪，整个特兰西瓦尼亚是匈牙利王室旗下的一个自治公国。在1241年和1242年鞑靼人对特兰西瓦尼亚进行毁灭性的袭击之后，匈牙利国王贝拉四世以免费的土地和税收优惠政策说服德国萨克森人在特兰西瓦尼亚定居。他想保卫王室的东南侧。他还授予塞凯利人--一个早先与马加尔人一起移居到该地区的匈牙利民族--自治权，以换取他们的军事支持。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "In the 14th century, Prince Basarab I (r 1310–52) united various political formations in the region south of the Carpathians to create the first Romanian principality – Wallachia, dubbed Ţara Românească (Romanian Land). Its indigenous peasantry became known as Vlachs."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "14世纪，巴萨拉布一世（Basarab I，1310-52年）将喀尔巴阡山脉以南地区的各种政治组织联合起来，建立了第一个罗马尼亚公国--瓦拉几亚，被称为Ţara Românească（罗马尼亚地）。其本土农民被称为瓦拉几人。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "Peasants dominated the populations of these medieval principalities. In Wallachia and Moldavia peasants were subjugated as serfs to the landed aristocracy (boyars), a hereditary class. There were some free, land-owning peasants (moşneni) too. The two principalities were ruled by a prince who was also the military leader. Most noblemen were Hungarian; the peasants were Romanians. After a 1437 peasant uprising in Transylvania, Magyar nobles formed a political alliance with the Székely and Saxon leaders. This Union of the Three Nations would later become the constitutional basis for government in Transylvania in the 16th century, but they would need to resist a powerful enemy in the East to reach that point."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "农民在这些中世纪公国的人口中占主导地位。在瓦拉几亚和摩尔达维亚，农民作为农奴受制于土地贵族（boyars），这是一个世袭的阶层。也有一些自由的、拥有土地的农民（moşneni）。这两个公国由一位王子统治，他也是军事领导人。大多数贵族是匈牙利人；农民是罗马尼亚人。1437年特兰西瓦尼亚的农民起义后，马扎尔贵族与塞克利和撒克逊领导人组成了政治联盟。这个三国联盟后来成为16世纪特兰西瓦尼亚政府的宪法基础，但他们需要抵抗东方的强大敌人才能达到这个目的。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_8", "Throughout the 14th and 15th centuries, Wallachia and Moldavia offered strong resistance to the Ottoman Empire’s northward expansion. Mircea cel Bătrân (Mircea the Old; r 1386–1418), Vlad Ţepeş (‘The Impaler’; r 1448, 1456–62, 1476), and Ştefan cel Mare (Stephen the Great; r 1457–1504) were legendary figures in this struggle. When the Turks conquered Hungary in the 16th century, Transylvania became a vassal of the Ottoman Empire, retaining its autonomy by paying tribute to the sultan. Catholicism and Protestantism were recognised as official state religions while the Orthodox faith of many Romanians remained an unofficial religion. Later, attempts were made to force them to convert to Catholicism."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_8", "在整个14和15世纪，瓦拉几亚和摩尔达维亚对奥斯曼帝国的向北扩张进行了强有力的抵抗。老米尔恰（1386-1418）、弗拉德·采佩什'穿刺者'（1448/1456-62/1476年）和斯蒂芬大帝（1457-1504年）是这场斗争的传奇人物。当土耳其人在16世纪征服匈牙利时，特兰西瓦尼亚成为奥斯曼帝国的附庸，通过向苏丹纳贡来保留其自治权。天主教和新教被定为国教，但是很多罗马尼亚人私下信仰东正教。后来，一些人尝试强迫他们皈依天主教。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_9", "After the Ottoman victory in Transylvania, Wallachia and Moldavia also paid tribute to the Turks but maintained their autonomy. In 1600 Wallachia and Moldavia were briefly united with Transylvania under Mihai Viteazul (Michael the Brave; r 1593–1601) at Alba Iulia. In order to fight Ottoman rule, he joined forces in 1594 with the ruling princes of Moldavia and Transylvania against the Turks, attacking strongholds and massacring Turks. In 1595 the Turks called a truce with Viteazul."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_9", "奥斯曼帝国在特兰西瓦尼亚取得胜利后，瓦拉几亚和摩尔达维亚也向土耳其人纳贡，但保持了自治。1600年，瓦拉几亚和摩尔达维亚与特兰西瓦尼亚在勇敢者米海尔（1593-1601年执政）的带领下在阿尔巴尤利亚短暂地联合起来。为了对抗奥斯曼帝国的统治，他在1594年与摩尔达维亚和特兰西瓦尼亚的执政王子联合起来对抗土耳其人，攻击据点并屠杀土耳其人。1595年，土耳其人与他停战。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_10", "The Transylvanian prince, Andrew Báthory, subsequently turned against the Wallachian prince and, on 28 October 1599, Mihai Viteazul defeated and killed Báthory’s troops near Sibiu. Viteazul declared himself the new prince of Transylvania, then in spring 1600 invaded Moldavia, where he was also crowned prince. This first political union of the three Romanian principalities lasted for slightly more than a year: Viteazul was defeated by a joint Habsburg-Transylvanian noble army just months later and in August 1601 he was captured and beheaded."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_10", "特兰西瓦尼亚亲王安德鲁-巴托里（Andrew Báthory）随后转向反对瓦拉几亚亲王，1599年10月28日，勇敢者米海尔在锡比乌附近击败并杀死了巴托里的军队。勇敢者宣布自己是特兰西瓦尼亚的新亲王，然后在1600年春天入侵摩尔达维亚，并在那里被加冕为亲王。这个罗马尼亚三个公国的第一次政治联盟持续了一年多的时间。仅仅几个月后，勇敢者就被哈布斯堡-特兰西瓦尼亚的一支联合贵族军队打败，1601年8月，他被抓获并被斩首。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_11", "In 1683 the Turks were defeated at the gates of Vienna and in 1687 Transylvania came under Habsburg rule. The 18th century marked the start of Transylvanian Romanians’ fight for political emancipation. Romanian peasants constituted 60% of the population, yet continued to be excluded from political life. In 1784 three serfs called Horea, Cloşca and Crişan led a major uprising. It was quashed, and its leaders were crushed to death, but on 22 August 1785 the Habsburg emperor, Joseph II, abolished serfdom in Transylvania."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_11", "1683年，土耳其人在维也纳门前被打败，1687年，特兰西瓦尼亚被哈布斯堡统治。18世纪是特兰西瓦尼亚罗马尼亚人争取政治解放的开始。罗马尼亚农民占人口的60%，但仍然被排除在政治生活之外。1784年，三个名叫霍雷亚、克洛斯卡和克里桑的农奴领导了一次大规模的起义。起义被镇压，其领导人被击毙，但在1785年8月22日，哈布斯堡皇帝约瑟夫二世在特兰西瓦尼亚废除了农奴制。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_12", "The 17th century in Wallachia was marked by the lengthy reign of Constantin Brâncoveanu (r 1688-1714), a period of relative peace and prosperity characterised by a great cultural and artistic renaissance. In 1775 part of Moldavia’s northern territory – Bucovina – was annexed by Austria-Hungary. This was followed in 1812 by the loss of its eastern territory – Bessarabia (most of which is in present-day Moldova) – to Russia. After the Russo-Turkish War of 1828-9, Wallachia and Moldavia became Russian protectorates while remaining in the Ottoman Empire."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_12", "17世纪的瓦拉几亚以康斯坦丁-布兰科瓦努（Constantin Brâncoveanu，1688-1714年）的长期统治为标志，这是一个相对和平和繁荣的时期，其特点是文化和艺术的伟大复兴。1775年，摩尔达维亚的部分北部领土--布科维纳--被奥匈帝国吞并。随后在1812年，其东部领土--比萨拉比亚（大部分位于今天的摩尔多瓦）--被俄罗斯夺走。在1828-9年的俄土战争之后，瓦拉几亚和摩尔达维亚成为俄罗斯的保护国，同时仍属于奥斯曼帝国。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_13", "In Transylvania the revolutionary spirit that gripped much of Europe in the years leading up to 1848 was entangled with the Wallachian revolution, which in Transylvania was led by Hungarian poet Sándor Petőfi. Hungarian revolutionaries sought an end to Habsburg domination of Hungary. Concurrently, Romanian revolutionaries demanded their political emancipation, equality and the abolition of serfdom, singing 'Deșteaptă-te române' meaning 'awaken, Romanian' - a message of liberty and patriotism that would go on to become the revolutionary national anthem of Romania."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_13", "在特兰西瓦尼亚，在1848年之前的几年里，革命精神笼罩着欧洲大部分地区，它与瓦拉几革命纠缠在一起，在特兰西瓦尼亚，瓦拉几革命由匈牙利诗人裴多菲·山陀儿领导。匈牙利革命者寻求结束哈布斯堡对匈牙利的统治。同时，罗马尼亚革命者要求他们的政治解放、平等和废除农奴制，唱着'Deșteaptă-te române'，意思是'觉醒吧，罗马尼亚人'--这个自由和爱国主义的信息，后来成为罗马尼亚的革命国歌。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_14", "The Austrian authorities struck a deal with Transylvania’s Romanians, promising them national recognition in return for joining forces with them against the Hungarian revolutionaries in Transylvania. Thus, Transylvanian Romanians fought against and enacted revenge upon Transylvanian Hungarians for what was perceived as centuries of mistreatment. Russian intervention finally quashed the Hungarian revolutionaries, ending a revolution that had shocked all sides by its escalation to civil war."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_14", "奥地利当局与特兰西瓦尼亚的罗马尼亚人达成了一项协议，承认他们国家的存在，以换取他们在镇压特兰西瓦尼亚的匈牙利革命者。因此，特兰西瓦尼亚的罗马尼亚人与特兰西瓦尼亚的匈牙利人进行了斗争，并对他们所认为的几个世纪的虐待行为进行了报复。俄罗斯的干预最终镇压了匈牙利革命者，结束了一场因升级为内战而震惊各方的革命。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_15", "In its aftermath, the region fell under direct rule of Austria-Hungary from Budapest. Ruthless ‘Magyarisation’ followed: Hungarian was established as the official language and any Romanians who dared oppose the regime. By contrast Wallachia and Moldavia prospered. In 1859, with French support, Alexandru Ioan Cuza was elected to the thrones of Moldavia and Wallachia, creating a national state known as the United Romanian Principalities on 11 December 1861, and thus, in 1862, Romania was born."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_15", "在其之后，该地区从匈牙利王国落入奥匈帝国的直接统治之下。无情的'马扎尔化'随之而来。匈牙利语被确立为官方语言，任何敢于反对该政权的罗马尼亚人都被残酷镇压。相比之下，瓦拉几亚和摩尔达维亚却很兴旺。1859年，在法国的支持下，亚历山德鲁 伊万 库扎当选为摩尔达维亚和瓦拉几亚国王位，于1861年12月11日创建了一个被称为罗马尼亚联合公国的民族国家，因此，在1862年，罗马尼亚诞生了。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_16", "The reform-minded Cuza was forced to abdicate in 1866 by mutinous army officers, and his place was taken by the Prussian prince Carol I. With Russian assistance, Romania declared independence from the Ottoman Empire in 1877. After the 1877–8 War of Independence, Dobrogea became part of Romania. Under the consequent Treaty of San Stefano and the Congress of Berlin in 1878, Romanian independence was recognised. In 1881 it was declared a kingdom and on 22 May 1881 Carol I was crowned the first king of Romania."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_16", "哗变的军官逼迫改革派国王退位，由普鲁士王子卡罗尔一世担任国王。在俄罗斯的帮助下，罗马尼亚于1877年宣布从奥斯曼帝国独立。1877-8年的独立战争后，多布罗加成为罗马尼亚的一部分。根据随后的《圣斯蒂法诺条约》和1878年的柏林会议，罗马尼亚的独立得到了承认。1881年，它被宣布为一个王国，1881年5月22日，卡罗尔一世被加冕为罗马尼亚的第一位国王。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_17", "Through shrewd political manoeuvring, Romania greatly benefited from WWI. Despite Romania having formed a secret alliance with Austria-Hungary in 1883, it began WWI with neutrality. In 1916, the government under Ion Brătianu declared war on Austria-Hungary. Its objective was to seize Transylvania from Austria-Hungary."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_17", "通过精明的政治手腕，罗马尼亚从一战中获益匪浅。尽管罗马尼亚在1883年与奥匈帝国结成了秘密联盟，但它在一战开始时仍保持中立。1916年，扬·康斯坦丁·布勒蒂亚努领导的政府向奥匈帝国宣战。它的目标是从奥匈帝国手中夺取特兰西瓦尼亚。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_18", "The defeat of Austria-Hungary in 1918 paved the way for the formation of modern Romania. Bessarabia, the area east of the Prut River which had been part of Moldavia until 1812 when it was taken by the Russians, was joined to Romania. Likewise, Bucovina, which had been in Austro-Hungarian hands since 1775, was also reunited with Romania. Part of the Austrian-Hungarian Banat, which had been incorporated in Romania, was also handed over. Furthermore, Transylvania was finally united with Romania. Hence, at the end of WWI, Romania – now known as Greater Romania – more than doubled its territory (from 120, 000 to 295, 000 sq km) and its population (from 7.5 to 16 million). The acquisition of this new territory was ratified by the Triple Entente powers in 1920 under the Treaty of Trianon."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_18", "1918年奥匈帝国的战败为现代罗马尼亚的形成铺平了道路。普鲁特河以东的比萨拉比亚地区在1812年被俄国人占领之前一直是摩尔达维亚的一部分，该地区被并入罗马尼亚。同样，自1775年以来一直在奥匈帝国手中的布科维纳，也与罗马尼亚重新结合。被纳入罗马尼亚的奥匈帝国巴纳特的部分地区也被移交。此外，特兰西瓦尼亚也最终与罗马尼亚统一了。因此，在一战结束时，罗马尼亚--现在被称为大罗马尼亚--的领土（从120,000平方公里到295,000平方公里）和人口（从750万到1600万）增加了一倍以上。1920年，三国协约国根据《特里亚侬条约》批准了对这块新领土的收购。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_19", "In the years leading up to WWII, Romania, under the able guidance of foreign minister Nicolae Titulescu, sought security in an alliance with France and Britain, and joined Yugoslavia and Czechoslovakia in the Little Entente. Romania also signed a Balkan Pact with Yugoslavia, Turkey and Greece, and later established diplomatic relations with the USSR. These efforts were weakened by the Western powers’ appeasement of Hitler and by Romania’s own King Carol II."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_19", "在二战之前的几年里，罗马尼亚在外交部长尼古拉-蒂图列斯库（Nicolae Titulescu）的干练指导下，在与法国和英国的联盟中寻求安全，并加入了南斯拉夫和捷克斯洛伐克的小协约。罗马尼亚还与南斯拉夫、土耳其和希腊签订了《巴尔干条约》，后来又与苏联建立了外交关系。这些努力因西方大国对希特勒的绥靖和罗马尼亚自己的国王卡罗尔二世而被削弱。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_20", "Carol II succeeded his father Ferdinand I to the throne. Extreme right-wing parties opposed to a democratic regime emerged, notably the anti-Semitic League of the National Christian Defence, which consequently gave birth to the Legion of the Archangel Michael in 1927. This notorious breakaway faction, better known as the fascist Iron Guard, was led by Corneliu Codreanu and by 1935 dominated the political scene. Finding himself unable to manipulate the political parties, Carol II declared a royal dictatorship in February 1938. All political parties were dissolved and laws were passed to halve the size of the electorate. Between 1939 and 1940 alone, Romania had no less than nine different governments."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_20", "卡罗尔二世继承了他父亲斐迪南一世的王位。反对民主政权的极端右翼政党出现了，特别是反犹太主义的全国基督教保卫联盟，该联盟因此在1927年诞生了大天使迈克尔军团。这个臭名昭著的分裂派别，也就是众所周知的法西斯铁卫，由科内留-科德雷阿努领导，到1935年主导了政治舞台。卡罗尔二世发现自己无法操纵各政党，于是在1938年2月宣布实行皇家独裁统治。所有政党被解散，并通过法律将选民人数减半。仅在1939年至1940年间，罗马尼亚就有不少于九届不同的政府。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_21", "In 1939 Carol II clamped down on the anti-Semitic Iron Guard, which until 1937 he had supported. Codreanu and 13 other legionaries were arrested, sentenced to 10 years’ imprisonment, and then assassinated. In revenge for their leader’s death, Iron Guard members murdered Carol II’s prime minister, Armand Călinescu, leading to the butchering of 252 Iron Guard members by Carol II’s forces. In accordance with the king’s wishes, the corpses were strung up in public squares. Only with the collapse of the Axis powers at the end of WWII did the Iron Guard disintegrate (in 1999, Codreanu’s nephew Nicador Zelea Codreanu tried unsuccessfully to revive the reviled group)."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_21", "1939年，卡罗尔二世对反犹太主义的铁卫队进行了镇压，直到1937年他还支持镇压。科德里亚努和其他13名军团成员被逮捕，被判处10年监禁，然后被暗杀。为了报复他们领导人的死亡，铁卫队成员谋杀了卡罗尔二世的总理阿尔芒-卡列斯库，导致卡罗尔二世的部队屠杀了252名铁卫队成员。根据国王的意愿，这些尸体被吊挂在公共广场上。直到二战结束轴心国崩溃，铁卫队才解体（1999年，科德里亚努的侄子尼卡多-泽拉-科德里亚努试图恢复这个被人唾弃的组织，但没有成功）"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_22", "Romania was isolated after the fall of France in May 1940, and in June 1940 Greater Romania collapsed in accordance with the Molotov-Ribbentrop Pact. The USSR re-occupied Bessarabia. On 30 August 1940 Romania was forced to cede northern Transylvania to Hungary by order of Nazi Germany and fascist Italy. In September 1940, Southern Dobrogea was given to Bulgaria."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_22", "1940年5月法国快速沦陷后，罗马尼亚被孤立，1940年6月大罗马尼亚根据《莫洛托夫-里宾特洛甫条约》瓦解了。苏联重新占领了比萨拉比亚。1940年8月30日，在纳粹德国和法西斯意大利的命令下，罗马尼亚被迫将特兰西瓦尼亚北部割让给匈牙利。1940年9月，南多布罗加被交给了保加利亚。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_23", "Not surprisingly, the loss of territories sparked widespread popular demonstrations. Even Carol II realised he could not quash the increasing mass hysteria and on the advice of one of his councillors, the king called in General Marshall Ion Antonescu. To defend the interests of the ruling classes, Antonescu forced King Carol II to abdicate in favour of the king’s 19-year-old son Michael. Antonescu then imposed a fascist dictatorship, with himself as conducător (supreme leader)."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_23", "毫不奇怪，领土的丧失引发了广泛的民众示威。即使是卡罗尔二世也意识到他无法平息日益严重的群众歇斯底里情绪，在他的一位议员的建议下，国王召见了马歇尔将军扬-安东内斯库。为了维护统治阶级的利益，安东尼斯库强迫国王卡罗尔二世退位，让给国王19岁的儿子米海尔。安东内斯库随后实行了法西斯独裁统治，他自己是最高领导人。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_24", "German troops were allowed to enter Romania in October 1940, and in June 1941 Antonescu joined Hitler’s anti-Soviet war. One of Antonescu’s aims in joining forces with Hitler was to recover Bessarabia and this was achieved in August 1941. The results of this Romanian-Nazi alliance were gruesome, with over 200, 000 Romanian Jews – mainly from newly regained Bessarabia –and 40, 000 Roma deported to transit camps in Transdniestr and murdered in Auschwitz. After the war, Antonescu was turned over to the Soviet authorities who condemned him to death in a show trial. Bessarabia fell back into Soviet hands."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_24", "1940年10月，德国军队被允许进入罗马尼亚，1941年6月，安东内斯库加入了希特勒的反苏战争。安东内斯库与希特勒联手的目的之一是收复比萨拉比亚，这在1941年8月实现了。这个罗马尼亚-纳粹联盟的结果是可怕的，超过20万罗马尼亚犹太人--主要来自新收复的比萨拉比亚--和4万罗姆人被驱逐到外德涅斯特的过渡营，并在奥斯威辛被杀害。战后，安东尼斯库被移交给了苏联。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_25", "As the war went badly and the Soviet army approached Romania’s borders, a rare national consensus was achieved. On 23 August 1944 an opportunistic Romania suddenly changed sides again, capturing the 53, 159 German soldiers who were stationed in Romania at the time, and declared war on Nazi Germany. By this dramatic act, Romania salvaged its independence and shortened the war. By 25 October, the Romanian and Soviet armies had driven the Hungarian and German forces from Transylvania, replacing the valued territory back under Romanian control. The costs, however, were appalling: 500, 000 Romanian soldiers died fighting for the Axis powers, and another 170, 000 died after Romania joined the Allies."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_25", "随着战争的发展，苏军逼近罗马尼亚的边界，一个罕见的民族共识得以实现。1944年8月23日，投机取巧的罗马尼亚突然再次改变立场，俘虏了当时驻扎在罗马尼亚的53159名德国士兵，并向纳粹德国宣战。通过这一戏剧性的行动，罗马尼亚挽救了它的独立，缩短了战争的时间。到10月25日，罗马尼亚和苏联军队将匈牙利和德国军队赶出了特兰西瓦尼亚，将这块有价值的领土重新置于罗马尼亚的控制之下。然而，其代价是惊人的。500，000名罗马尼亚士兵为轴心国作战而死亡，另外170，000人在罗马尼亚加入盟国后死亡。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_26", "Of all the countries that burst forward into the mass-industrialised, communist experiment in the 20th century, Romania and Russia were the most ill-prepared, both being overwhelmingly rural, agricultural countries. Prior to 1945, Romania’s Communist Party had no more than 1000 members. Its postwar ascendancy, which saw membership soar to 710,000 by 1947, was a consequence of backing from Moscow. The Soviet-engineered return of Transylvania greatly enhanced the prestige of the left-wing parties, which won the parliamentary elections in November 1946. A year later Prime Minister Petru Groza forced King Michael to abdicate (allegedly by holding the queen mother at gunpoint), the monarchy was abolished, and a Romanian People’s Republic proclaimed."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_26", "1945年之前，罗马尼亚的共产党员不超过1000人。战后，由于莫斯科的支持，其党员人数在1947年飙升至71万人。苏联策划的特兰西瓦尼亚的回归极大地提高了左翼政党的威望，他们在1946年11月的议会选举中获胜。一年后，总理佩特鲁-格罗扎迫使米海尔国王退位，君主制被废除，罗马尼亚人民共和国宣布成立。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_27", "A period of terror ensued in which all the prewar leaders, prominent intellectuals and suspected dissidents were imprisoned or interned in hard-labour camps. The most notorious prisons were in Piteşti, Gherla, Sighetu Marmaţiei and Aiud. Factories and businesses were nationalised, and in 1953 a new Slavicised orthography was introduced to obliterate all Latin roots of the Romanian language, while street and town names were changed to honour Soviet figures. Braşov was renamed Oraşul Stalin."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_27", "工厂和企业被国有化，1953年引入了新的斯拉夫化正字法，抹去了罗马尼亚语的所有拉丁语根，而街道和城镇的名字也被改为纪念苏联人物。布拉索夫被重新命名为斯大林市。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_28", "Romania’s loyalty to Moscow continued only until the late 1950s. Soviet troops were withdrawn from Romania in 1958, and street and town names were changed once more to emphasise the country’s Roman heritage. After 1960 Romania adopted an independent foreign policy under two ‘national’ communist leaders, Gheorghe Gheorghiu-Dej (leader from 1952 to 1965) and his protégé Nicolae Ceauşescu (from 1965 to 1989), both of whom had been imprisoned during WWII. Under these figures the concept of a great Romanian socialist state was flaunted."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_28", "罗马尼亚对莫斯科的忠诚只持续到50年代末。苏联军队于1958年从罗马尼亚撤出，街道和城镇的名称再次被改变，以强调该国的罗马遗产。1960年后，罗马尼亚在两位 ‘民族’共产主义领导人格奥尔基-格奥尔基乌-德伊（1952年至1965年的领导人）和他的门徒尼古拉-齐奥塞斯库（1965年至1989年）的领导下采取了独立的外交政策，这两人在二战期间都曾被监禁。在这些人物的领导下，一个伟大的罗马尼亚社会主义国家的概念被标榜出来。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_29", "Romania never broke completely with the USSR, but Ceauşescu refused to assist the Soviets in their 1968 ‘intervention’ in Czechoslovakia. His public condemnation of it earned him praise and economic aid from the West. In 1975 Romania was granted ‘most favoured nation’ status by the USA, which yielded more than US$1 billion in US-backed credits in the decade that followed. And when Romania condemned the Soviet invasion in Afghanistan and participated in the 1984 Los Angeles Olympic Games despite a Soviet-bloc boycott, Ceauşescu was officially decorated by Great Britain’s Queen Elizabeth II."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_29", "罗马尼亚从未与苏联彻底决裂，但齐奥塞斯库拒绝协助苏联在1968年对捷克斯洛伐克的'干预'。他的公开谴责为他赢得了西方的赞誉和经济援助。1975年，罗马尼亚被美国授予‘最惠国待遇’的地位，在随后的十年中，美国支持的信贷超过10亿美元。当罗马尼亚谴责苏联对阿富汗的入侵，并不顾苏联集团的抵制参加1984年洛杉矶奥运会时，齐奥塞斯库得到了英国女王伊丽莎白二世的正式授勋。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_30", "Meanwhile, Romanians suffered painfully during the 25-year dictatorship of Nicolae Ceauşescu and his family. Thousands were imprisoned or repressed by the much-feared secret police (Securitate), huge amounts of money were squandered on megalomaniacal, grandiose projects and the population lived in abject poverty."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_30", "与此同时，罗马尼亚人在尼古拉-齐奥塞斯库（Nicolae Ceauşescu）及其家族25年的独裁统治期间饱受痛苦。数以千计的人被监禁或被令人恐惧的秘密警察（Securitate）镇压，大量的资金被挥霍在自大狂、宏伟的项目上，人们生活在赤贫之中。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_31", "In late 1989, as the world watched the collapse of one communist regime after another, it seemed only a matter of time before Romania’s turn would come. The Romanian revolution was carried out with Latin passion and intensity, and of all the Soviet Bloc countries, only Romania’s government transfer ended with a dead leader."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_31", "1989年末，当世界看到一个又一个共产主义政权的崩溃时，似乎迟早会轮到罗马尼亚。罗马尼亚的革命包含了拉丁民族情绪。在所有的苏联集团国家中，只有罗马尼亚的政权更迭以一个死去的领导人结束。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_32", "Summise to say, a marked history of emergencies has proven that it takes but a spark to ignite an unbridled fervour in Romania's people, rising up time and time again to defend themselves to heed the call of: 'Awaken, Romanian'."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ROMANIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_32", "总结来说，一段明显的突发事件的历史证明，只需要一个火花就能点燃罗马尼亚人民肆无忌惮的热情，一次又一次地站起来捍卫自己，听从号召。'觉醒吧，罗马尼亚人'。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_BUILDINGS_PAGE_BUILDING_CVS_ROMANIA_UI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "Declared historic monuments by the Romanian Culture Ministry to mark Romanian heritage, Fortăreață (meaning 'Fortress') can be found almost everywhere in Romania in one form or another; with as many as 28 in a single county. Some of the more well-known castles are surrounded by breathtaking landscapes and legendary myths of the people that occupied them. In the Transylvania region, many Fortăreață serve as churches that were established by Saxons between the 13th and 16th centuries, but the majority of these fortresses today serve as some of Romania's finest museums dedicated to the country's or region's storied history."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_BUILDINGS_PAGE_BUILDING_CVS_ROMANIA_UI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "被罗马尼亚文化部宣布为历史遗迹的堡垒（Fortăreață，意为 ‘要塞’）在罗马尼亚几乎随处可见，其形式各异；一个县就有多达28座。一些比较知名的城堡有惊艳的风景和居住者留下的传奇故事。在特兰西瓦尼亚地区，许多堡垒曾今是13至16世纪撒克逊人建立的教堂，但这些堡垒中的大多数今天都成为罗马尼亚最好的博物馆，专门展示该国或该地区的传奇历史。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_UNITS_PAGE_UNIT_CVS_ROMANIA_UU_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "The Vânători de Munte ('Mountain Huntsmen') are the elite mountain troops of the Romanian Land Forces, first established as an independent army corps in 1916 during World War I. They continued to serve during World War II on the Eastern Front in some of the harshest battles, including the sieges of Sevastopol and Stalingrad where their performance lived up to their reputation. Virtually all of their commanders from brigade level and up received the Knight's Cross of the Iron Cross. The greatest single achievement of the Vânători de Munte was the capture of Nalchik on 2 November 1942, the farthest point of Axis advance into the Caucasus. At the end of the war, one of the first measures taken by the Soviets in occupied Romania was to disband the mountain troops. However, shortly after Soviet occupation ended, the Vânători de Munte we re-established as a distinct branch of the Romanian Land Forces where they continue to operate to this day."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_UNITS_PAGE_UNIT_CVS_ROMANIA_UU_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "Vânători de Munte（‘山地猎手’）是罗马尼亚陆军的精锐山地部队，在第一次世界大战期间于1916年作为独立军团首次成立。他们几乎所有的旅级以上的指挥官都获得了铁十字骑士勋章。Vânători de Munte最伟大的成就是在1942年11月2日占领了纳尔奇克，这是轴心国进入高加索地区的最远点。战争结束后，苏联人在被占领的罗马尼亚采取的第一批措施之一就是解散山地部队。然而，在苏联占领结束后不久，我们重新建立了Vânători de Munte，作为罗马尼亚陆军的一个独立分支，他们继续在那里行动至今。"),
("en_US", "LOC_LEADER_CVS_VLAD_III_NAME", "Vlad III"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_LEADER_CVS_VLAD_III_NAME", "弗拉德三世"),
("en_US", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_CVS_VLAD_III_UA_NAME", "House of Drăculești"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_CVS_VLAD_III_UA_NAME", "德拉库勒斯蒂王室"),
("en_US", "LOC_UNIT_CVS_VLAD_III_UU_NAME", "Călăraşi"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_UNIT_CVS_VLAD_III_UU_NAME", "卡拉拉西"),
("en_US", "LOC_AGENDA_CVS_VLAD_III_NAME", "Scorched Earth"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_AGENDA_CVS_VLAD_III_NAME", "焦土"),
("en_US", "LOC_AGENDA_CVS_VLAD_III_DESCRIPTION", "Will join wars and pillage wherever possible and respects those that do the same. Views neighboring civilizations with a small military as opportunities for conquest."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_AGENDA_CVS_VLAD_III_DESCRIPTION", "尽可能加入战争和掠夺，并尊重那些做同样事情的人。将拥有少量军队的邻近文明视为征服对象。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_LEADER_CVS_VLAD_III_REASON_ANY", "(You have pillaged a high number of tiles.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_LEADER_CVS_VLAD_III_REASON_ANY", "（你掠夺了很多单元格）"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_CVS_VLAD_III_HAPPY", "Vlad III respects your pillaging tactics"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_CVS_VLAD_III_HAPPY", "弗拉德尊重您的劫掠战术"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_LEADER_CVS_VLAD_III_REASON_ANY", "(You are neighbors and have a weak army.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_LEADER_CVS_VLAD_III_REASON_ANY", "（您与邻居军队羸弱）"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_CVS_VLAD_III_UNHAPPY", "Vlad III sees your weak military as an opportunity for conquest"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_CVS_VLAD_III_UNHAPPY", "弗拉基米尔三世将你们薄弱的军队视为征服的机会"),
