("en_US", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_ADJECTIVE", "Siamese"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_ADJECTIVE", "暹罗的"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_DESCRIPTION_JFD_CIVILIZATION", "Siamese Civilization"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_DESCRIPTION_JFD_CIVILIZATION", "暹罗文明"),
("en_US", "LOC_TRAIT_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SRI_AYUTTHAYA_NAME", "Sri Ayutthaya"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_TRAIT_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SRI_AYUTTHAYA_NAME", "大城府"),
("en_US", "LOC_UNIT_SUK_SIAM_CHANGSUEK_NAME", "Chang Suek"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_UNIT_SUK_SIAM_CHANGSUEK_NAME", "暹罗战象"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_UNITS_PAGE_UNIT_SUK_SIAM_CHANGSUEK_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "In Southeast Asia elephants continued to be employed in warfare far into the Middle Ages. In Siam, particularly, Chang Suek, or war elephants were highly prized. Three people would be stationed on each war elephant, one riding on the neck to do battle, one in the middle to pass weapons such as halberds, spears and javelins to the first and one person at the back to control the elephant. Even Siamese leaders would fight in battle on war elephants, indeed, King Ramkhamhaeng, King Naresuan and the consort of King Maha Chakkraphat, Sri Suriyothai have all fought atop Chang Suek."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_UNITS_PAGE_UNIT_SUK_SIAM_CHANGSUEK_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "在中世纪的东南亚，大象持续被用于战争。特别是在暹罗战象受到高度重视。每头战象上都有三个人，一个骑在脖子上作战，一个在中间把武器如戟、矛和标枪传给第一个人，一个人在背上控制大象。即使是暹罗的领导人也会在战象上作战，事实上，兰甘亨国王、纳黎萱国王和摩诃·查克腊帕国王的妃子素丽瑶泰都曾在战象上面作战。"),
("en_US", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_CHANGSUEK_NAME", "White Elephant"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_CHANGSUEK_NAME", "白象"),
("en_US", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_CHANGSUEK_DESCRIPTION", "Adjacent units gain double experience from battles."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_CHANGSUEK_DESCRIPTION", "相邻单位获得双倍作战经验。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DISTRICT_SUK_FLOATINGMARKET_NAME", "Floating Market"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DISTRICT_SUK_FLOATINGMARKET_NAME", "水上市场"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_DISTRICTS_PAGE_DISTRICT_SUK_FLOATINGMARKET_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "In the past the areas adjacent to the rivers were the first to be populated. Thus most communities of Thailand were built at the sides of rivers. The waterways served as means of transportation and the center of economic activity as well. Boats were mainly used for both local and regional trade, bringing goods from those that produced to those that could barter and trade. Such heavy reliance on boats in riverside communities, especially in the Chao Phraya River Basin, helped increase the number of floating markets and allowed them to serve as hubs for the communities in Central Thailand for centuries."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_DISTRICTS_PAGE_DISTRICT_SUK_FLOATINGMARKET_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "在过去，临近河流的地区是最早的居民区。因此，泰国的大多数社区都建在河流的两旁。水路是运输渠道，也是经济活动的中心。船只主要用于当地和地区的贸易，把生产者的货物带到那些可以进行易货贸易的地方。在河边社区，特别是在湄南河流域，这种对船只数量的增加推动了水上市场的数量的增加，并使其在几个世纪内成为泰国中部社区的中心。"),
("en_US", "LOC_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_NAME", "Ramkhamhaeng"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_NAME", "兰甘亨"),
("en_US", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_SUK_THE_THAI_ALPHABET_NAME", "The Thai Alphabet"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_SUK_THE_THAI_ALPHABET_NAME", "泰语字母表"),
("en_US", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_FATHER_GOVERNS_CHILDREN_NAME", "Father Governs Children"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_FATHER_GOVERNS_CHILDREN_NAME", "君父统治"),
("en_US", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_FATHER_GOVERNS_CHILDREN_DESCRIPTION", "Likes civilizations with who have cultured and happy citizens. Is upset by civilizations that do not attend to their citizens’ happiness"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_FATHER_GOVERNS_CHILDREN_DESCRIPTION", "喜欢文化和宜居度高的文明，厌恶不注重人民宜居度的文明。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_REASON_ANY", "(You have cultured and happy citizens.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_REASON_ANY", "（你的人民有文化又很快乐）"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_FATHER_GOVERNS_CHILDREN_HAPPY", "Ramkhamhaeng is pleased you have cultured and happy citizens"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_FATHER_GOVERNS_CHILDREN_HAPPY", "兰甘亨觉得你的人民有文化又快乐。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_REASON_ANY", "(Your empire is unhappy.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_REASON_ANY", "（你的帝国很不欢乐）"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_FATHER_GOVERNS_CHILDREN_UNHAPPY", "Ramkhamhaeng is concerned that your people are unhappy"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_FATHER_GOVERNS_CHILDREN_UNHAPPY", "兰甘亨觉得你的帝国很不高兴。"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_NAME", "Vieng Chan"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_NAME", "万象"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_FRONTEND_NAME", "Vieng Chan"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_FRONTEND_NAME", "万象"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_DESCRIPTION", "Vieng Chan city-state"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_DESCRIPTION", "万象城邦"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_ADJECTIVE", "Vieng Chan"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_ADJECTIVE", "万象的"),
("en_US", "LOC_LEADER_TRAIT_AYUTTHAYA_NAME", "Vieng Chan Suzerain Bonus"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_LEADER_TRAIT_AYUTTHAYA_NAME", "万象宗主国加成"),
("en_US", "LOC_CITY_NAME_AYUTTHAYA", "Vieng Chan"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CITY_NAME_AYUTTHAYA", "万象"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CITYSTATES_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "Set on a bend in the Mekong River, Vieng Chan (much more commonly known as Vientiane because that’s how the French wrote it down) was first settled around the 9th century AD and formed part of one of the early Lao valley mueang (city-states) that were consolidated around the 10th century under the control of the Khmer empire. The Lao who settled here did so because the surrounding alluvial plains were so fertile, and initially Vieng Chan prospered and enjoyed a fragile sovereignty following the decline of Angkor. In the ensuing centuries, Vieng Chan’s fortunes have been mixed. At various times it has been a major regional centre; at other times it has been controlled by the Vietnamese, Burmese and Siamese."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CITYSTATES_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "万象（Vieng Chan）位于湄公河的一个转弯处，最早在公元9世纪左右定居，形成了早期佬人河谷城邦的一部分，这些城邦在10世纪左右在高棉帝国的控制下被巩固。佬人在这里定居是因为周围的冲积平原非常肥沃，在吴哥王朝衰落后，最初万象繁荣并享有脆弱的主权。在随后的几个世纪里，万象的命运好坏参半。在不同时期，它是一个主要的区域中心；在其他时候，它被越南人、缅甸人和暹罗人控制。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CITYSTATES_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "The height of Vieng Chan’s success was probably in the years after it became the Lan Xang capital in the mid-16th century, after King Setthathirat moved the capital from Luang Prabang. Several of Vieng Chan’s wats were built following this shift and the city became a major centre of Buddhist learning. It didn’t last. Periodic invasions by the Burmese, Siamese and Chinese, and the eventual division of the Lan Xang kingdom took their toll on the city."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CITYSTATES_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "万象的巅峰时期可能是在16世纪中叶，萨特哈赛赖特国王将首都从琅勃拉邦迁出后，万象成为澜沧的首都后的几年。万象的几座寺庙都是在这一转变之后建造的，该城市成为了一个主要的佛教学习中心。但这并不持久。缅甸人、暹罗人和中国人的定期入侵，以及澜沧王国的最终分裂，都给该城市带来了损失。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CITYSTATES_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "It wasn’t until the Siamese installed Chao Anouvong, a Lao prince who had been educated in Bangkok, on the throne in 1805 that the city received an overdue makeover. Chao Anouvong’s public works included Wat Si Saket, built between 1819 and 1824. Unfortunately, Chao Anouvong’s attempts to assert Lao independence over the Siamese resulted in the most violent and destructive episode in Vieng Chan’s history. In 1828 the Siamese defeated Chao Anouvong’s armies and wasted no time in razing the city and carting off much of the population. Wat Si Saket, the base for the Thai invaders, was the only major building to survive, and the city was abandoned."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CITYSTATES_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "直到暹罗人在1805年将曾在曼谷受教育的老挝王子昭阿奴扶上王位，这座城市才得到了早该进行的改造。昭阿奴的公共工程包括沙格庙，建于1819至1824年。不幸的是，昭阿奴试图在暹罗人面前宣布老挝的独立，这导致了万象历史上最暴力和破坏性的事件。1828年，暹罗人打败了昭阿奴的军队，并不失时机地将城市夷为平地，将大部分人口运走。沙格庙是泰国入侵者的基地，是唯一幸存的主要建筑，城市被遗弃了。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CITYSTATES_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "Vieng Chan was in great disrepair, depopulated and disappearing into the forest, when the French arrived. It eventually passed to French rule in 1893. It became the capital of the French protectorate of Laos in 1899. The French rebuilt the city and rebuilt or repaired Buddhist temples such as Pha That Luang, Haw Phra Kaew, and left many colonial buildings behind. During French rule, the Vietnamese were encouraged to migrate to Laos, which resulted in 53% of the population of Vieng Chan being Vietnamese in the year of 1943. As late as 1945, the French drew up an ambitious plan to move massive Vietnamese population to three key areas, i.e. the Vientiane Plain, Savannakhet region, Bolaven Plateau, which was only discarded by Japanese invasion of Indochina. If this plan had been implemented, according to Martin Stuart-Fox, the Lao might well have lost control over their own country."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CITYSTATES_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_AYUTTHAYA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "法国人到达时，万象已经非常破败，人口减少，并消失在森林中。它最终在1893年被法国统治。1899年，它成为法国保护国老挝的首都。法国人重建了城市，重建或修复了佛教寺庙，如塔銮寺、玉佛寺，并留下了许多殖民时期的建筑。在法国统治期间，越南人被鼓励迁移到老挝，这导致在1943年，万象的人口中有53%是越南人。迟至1945年，法国人制定了一个雄心勃勃的计划，将大量的越南人口迁移到三个关键地区，即万象平原、沙湾拿吉地区、	布拉万高原，该计划在日本入侵印度支那后才被放弃。据马丁·斯图尔特·福克斯说，如果这个计划得以实施，老挝人很可能失去对自己国家的控制。"),
