("en_US", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SIAM_LOCATION", "Asia"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SIAM_LOCATION", "亚洲"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SIAM_SIZE", "Est. 198 thousand square miles (513.1 thousand square km)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SIAM_SIZE", "Est. 19.8万平方英里（513.1万平方公里）"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SIAM_POPULATION", "67.9 million (2015 est.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SIAM_POPULATION", "6790万（2015年估计）。"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SIAM_CAPITAL", "Various (Sukhothai, Phitsanulok, Ayutthaya, Lopburi, Thonburi, and currently Krung Thep/Bangkok)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SIAM_CAPITAL", "多个（素可泰、彭世洛、阿瑜陀耶、华富里、吞武里和曼谷）"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "Located in Southeast Asia between Burma (a.k.a. Myanmar), Laos, Cambodia and Malaysia, Siam - now Thailand - has a long and storied history. A beautiful and mysterious land of dark forests and ancient mountains, Siam has seen occupation and revolution, flood and famine, and the rise and fall of empires."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "暹罗——现在的泰国——位于东南亚，在缅甸、老挝、柬埔寨和马来西亚之间，有着悠久的历史和传奇的故事。暹罗是一片美丽而神秘的土地，有着黑暗的森林和古老的山脉，它经历了占领和革命、洪水和饥荒，以及帝国的兴衰。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "The earliest known settlers of Siam spoke Mon-Khmer languages. There were several different groups on the southeast Asia peninsula. One, the Mon, were known to have accepted Buddhism as far back as the sixth century AD. Another group, the Khmer, were primarily located in Cambodia, their capital at Angkor (home of Angkor Wat); in the 12th century they possessed an empire stretching over half of modern Thailand. The Khmer tended to follow Hinduism rather than Buddhism."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "已知最早的暹罗定居者讲勐-高棉语。东南亚半岛上有几个不同的群体。一个是勐族，已知早在公元六世纪就已经接受了佛教。另一个族群，高棉人，主要分布在柬埔寨，他们的首都在吴哥（吴哥窟所在地）；在12世纪，他们拥有的帝国延伸到了现代泰国的一半。高棉人倾向于信奉印度教而不是佛教。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "Around 1,000 AD the area saw an influx of Tai-speaking people called the 'Tai.' Modern historians generally believe that the Tai originated in northern Vietnam. In a few centuries the Tai had spread across much of Southeast Asia, as far west as northeastern India and as far south as the Malay Peninsula. By the 13th century the Tai were numerous enough to threaten the Mon and Khmer primacy in Siam."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "公元1000年左右，该地区涌入了讲泰语的人，称为“泰族”（傣族）。现代历史学家普遍认为，泰族人起源于越南北部。在几个世纪里，泰族已经遍布东南亚的大部分地区，最西边到印度东北部，最南边到马来半岛。到了13世纪，泰族的数量足以威胁到暹罗的孟族和高棉族的首要地位。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "In the mid-thirteenth century a Tai ruler successfully revolted against the Khmer Empire, founding the Sukhothai kingdom. It remained a small, unimportant power until the ascension of its third ruler, Ramkhamhaeng, in 1279. In twenty short years this extraordinary leader would transform the small kingdom of Sukhothai into a major regional power."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "十三世纪中期，一位泰族统治者成功地反抗了高棉帝国，建立了素可泰王国。它仍然是一个不重要的小国，直到1279年它的第三位统治者兰甘亨（Ramkhamhaeng）登基。在短短的20年里，这位非凡的领导人将素可泰这个小王国转变为一个主要的地区性强国。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "During his reign Ramkhamhaeng expanded his kingdom’s dominance west into Burma, east into Laos, and south down the Malay Peninsula. The king was a shrewd diplomat as well as a warlord; many territories joined his confederation voluntarily. Towards the end of his rule Ramkhamhaeng had a stone inscribed detailing his triumphs. It portrays a wealthy, contented kingdom ruled by a loving and benevolent monarch. Ramkhamhaeng died in 1298."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "兰甘亨在位期间，将其王国的统治权向西扩展到缅甸，向东扩展到老挝，向南扩展到马来半岛。这位国王是一位精明的外交家，也是一位军阀；许多地区自愿加入他的联盟。在他的统治即将结束时，兰甘亨在一块石头上刻下了他的胜利的细节。它描绘了一个由慈爱和仁慈的君主统治的富裕、满足的王国。拉姆康亨于1298年去世。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "Sukhothai would last a century past its greatest leader’s death before being consumed by Ayutthaya, a new Tai power rising in the south."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "素可泰在其最伟大的领导人去世后持续了一个世纪，然后被南方崛起的泰族新势力阿瑜陀耶所吞噬。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "The kingdom of Ayutthaya was founded by Ramathibodi I in 1351 on the Chao Phraya River Basin, a fertile plain just north of modern Bangkok. The kingdom was formed on the remains of an earlier kingdom, Lavo. In 1352 King Ramathibodi attacked the Khmer, driving them east out of Siam. By 1387 Ayutthaya was strong enough to attack north, conquering Sukhothai. And in 1431 the kingdom attacked the Khmer once more, this time capturing and sacking the capital city of Angkor after a seven-month siege."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "阿瑜陀耶王国是由拉玛铁菩提一世於1351年在昭披耶河流域建立的，湄南河流域是一片肥沃的平原，就在现代曼谷的北部。该王国是在早期王国罗斛（Lavo）的遗址上形成的。1352年，拉玛铁菩提国王袭击了高棉人，将他们赶出了暹罗的东部。到了1387年，阿瑜陀耶已经强大到可以向北进攻，征服了素可泰。1431年，阿瑜陀耶再次向高棉人发动攻击，在经过7个月的围攻后，夺取并洗劫了首都吴哥城。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_8", "By all accounts the city of Ayutthaya was beautiful and wealthy. It was traversed by a series of north-south canals which brought water to all sections of the city. The remains of magnificent palaces and temples can be seen in the city today. The Tai of Ayutthaya were the first people in the area to be called 'Siamese', and this of course eventually became the name of the entire country."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_8", "从各方面来看，阿瑜陀耶的城市都是美丽而富有的。它被一系列南北向的运河所穿过，这些运河将水带到城市的各个部分。今天，在这座城市可以看到宏伟的宫殿和寺庙的遗迹。大城的泰人是该地区第一个被称为“暹罗人”的人，当然，这也最终成为整个国家的名称。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_9", "From the Khmer, the Ayutthayans adopted the belief in the divinity of the king. The king was above all people. None could gaze upon his face, except for members of the royal family. In addition to the king’s increased religious/ceremonial power, King Trailok (1448-1488) reorganized the state to concentrate political power in the hands of the monarchy as well."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_9", "从高棉人那里，阿瑜陀耶人采纳了国王的神性信仰。国王高于所有的人。除了王室成员之外，没有人可以注视他的脸。除了国王的宗教/礼仪权力增加外，特莱洛国王（1448-1488）还重组了国家，将政治权力也集中在君主手中。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_10", "Socially, the Ayutthayans lived under a rigid caste system that assigned a numerical value to each person according to his or her rank. A slave was worth five units (called 'sakdi na'), a freeman 25 or so, and the heir to the throne perhaps 100,000 units. (The king himself was probably worth a gazillion - or even more!) Both Buddhism and Hinduism were followed in the country."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_10", "在社会上，阿瑜陀耶人生活在一个严格的种姓制度下，该制度根据每个人的等级分配一个数字值。一个奴隶值5个单位（称为 “sakdi na”），一个自由人值25个左右，而王位继承人可能值100,000个。(国王本人的价值可能是一百万——甚至更多！）该国同时信奉佛教和印度教。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_11", "Having dealt with Sukhothai to the north and Khmer to the southeast, the greatest threat to Ayutthaya lay in Burma, to the west. In 1569 Ayutthaya was overrun and conquered by Burma. It regained its independence at the end of the 16th century. Burmese troops once again sacked the city in 1767. This time they deported the royal family, burned the city to the ground, and destroyed all of the Ayutthayan works of art and historical records. The Kingdom never recovered from this attack. However a new Siamese kingdom would rapidly rise to power in Ayutthaya’s ashes."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_11", "在解决了北面的素可泰和东南面的高棉之后，对阿瑜陀耶的最大威胁是西面的缅甸。1569年，阿瑜陀耶被缅甸占领并征服了。它在16世纪末重新获得了独立。1767年，缅甸军队再次洗劫了该城。这一次，他们驱逐了王室成员，将城市烧为平地，并摧毁了所有阿瑜陀耶的艺术作品和历史记录。该王国从未从这次攻击中恢复过来。然而，一个新的暹罗王国将在阿瑜陀耶的灰烬中迅速崛起。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_12", "In 1767 (the same year that saw the final destruction of Ayutthaya), a Tai leader named 'Taksin' founded a new capital city at Thon Buri, some forty miles downstream from Ayutthaya (near present-day Bangkok). Built on the eastern side of the Chao Phraya River, the city was easier to defend from Burmese forces; located closer to the open sea, the city was ideally suited to accommodate international trade as well. In fact Taksin encouraged Chinese merchants to establish businesses in Thon Buri, and tax revenue from this trade was used to rebuild the Siamese economy, devastated from the recent Burmese attack."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_12", "1767年（同年，阿瑜陀耶最终被摧毁），一位名叫 “郑信”的泰族领袖在阿瑜陀耶下游约40英里处（靠近今天的曼谷）建立了一个新的首都——吞武里。该城建在湄南河的东侧，更容易抵御缅甸军队的进攻；该城更靠近海岸，非常适合容纳国际贸易。事实上，郑信鼓励中国商人在吞武里建立商管，而这些贸易的税收被用来重建暹罗的经济，因为暹罗在当时的缅甸袭击中遭到了破坏。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_13", "Taking advantage of his country’s wealth, Taksin constructed a powerful army and began expanding its territory. After retaking the territory that had belonged to Sukhothai and Ayutthaya, Taksin’s troops conquered additional territory in Laos, and pushed the Burmese forces out of traditional Tai lands to the north. In 1782 Taksin began showing signs of serious mental illness and was overthrown and killed. He was succeeded by a general named 'Chao Phraya Chakri' (he later changed his name to Rama I). The Chakri dynasty has remained in power in Thailand until today."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_13", "郑信利用其国家的财富，建立了一支强大的军队，并开始扩大其领土。在夺回属于素可泰和阿瑜陀耶的领土后，郑信的军队又征服了老挝的领土，并将缅甸军队赶出了北部的传统泰族土地。1782年，郑信开始出现严重的精神疾病迹象，并被推翻和杀害。他的继任者是一位名叫 “昭披耶却克里 ”的将军（后来他改名为拉玛一世）。却克里王朝一直在泰国执政，直到今天。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_14", "Shortly after assuming the throne, the new king moved his capital to Bangkok, a small village across the Chao Phraya River. Bangkok quickly grew into a bustling trading city, largely due to the many Chinese who immigrated to the metropolis."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_14", "就任后不久，新国王将首都迁至湄南河对面的一个小村庄——曼谷。曼谷迅速发展成为一个繁华的贸易城市，这主要是由于许多中国人移民到了这个大都市。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_15", "King Rama I and his successors continued to expand Siamese power into Laos and south down the Malay Peninsula. They also continued to clash with Burma, who remained a perennial menace until that country in turn was menaced by Great Britain (approaching from India)."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_15", "拉玛一世和他的继任者继续将暹罗的势力扩展到老挝和马来半岛的南部。他们还继续与缅甸发生冲突，缅甸仍然是一个常年的威胁，直到这个国家反过来受到英国的威胁。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_16", "King Rama I was also a great patron of Siamese culture, religion and the law. He rebuilt Siamese temples and palaces, and he greatly updated the Siamese legal system. His successor, Rama III (ruled 1809-24) was a patron of the arts, and no mean poet himself."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_16", "拉玛一世国王也是暹罗文化、宗教和法律的伟大支持者。他重建了暹罗的寺庙和宫殿，并大大更新了暹罗的法律体系。他的继任者拉玛三世（1809-24年在位）是一位艺术赞助人，他本人也是一位出色的诗人。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_17", "Perhaps the greatest triumph of Siamese diplomacy was that it avoided occupation by Western powers, unlike every other country in Southeast Asia. In 1826 Siam signed a treaty with Great Britain, and in 1855 this was expanded to allow the British unrestricted - and untaxed! - trade in Siamese ports. The British also secured the right to set up separate law courts to try cases involving British subjects. This was a humiliating loss of sovereignty and income for Siam, but it kept Britain from invading and occupying the country, and Siam soon signed similar treaties with other European powers and the United States."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_17", "也许暹罗外交的最大胜利是它避免了西方列强的占领，与东南亚的其他国家不同。1826年，暹罗与英国签署了一项条约，1855年，该条约被扩大，允许英国人在暹罗港口进行不受限制的——而且不征税！这就是暹罗的外交。在暹罗的港口进行贸易。英国人还获得了设立单独的法庭来审理涉及英国人的案件的权利。这对暹罗来说是一个屈辱的主权和收入损失，但它使英国没有入侵和占领这个国家，而且暹罗很快与其他欧洲国家和美国签署了类似的条约。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_18", "King Rama IV (ruled 1851 - 1868) was a keen student of the West. In some ways King Rama IV was rather enlightened for that place and time. A former Buddhist monk before assuming the throne, he sought to reform Buddhism in the country, which he believed had become corrupt and filled with superstition. He also began to remake the Siamese monarchy, removing from it the more onerous trappings of godhood. Although he remained largely an absolute ruler, at least his subjects were allowed to look directly at him."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_18", "拉玛四世国王（1851-1868年在位）是一位热衷于学习西方的人。在某些方面，拉玛四世国王在那个地方和那个时代是相当开明的。在登上王位之前，他曾是一名佛教僧侣，他试图在国内改革佛教，他认为佛教已经变得腐败并充满了迷信。他还开始重塑暹罗的君主制度，从它身上去除更多繁琐的神的外衣。虽然他在很大程度上仍然是一个绝对的统治者，但至少他的臣民被允许直视他。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_19", "King Rama IV’s son, Rama V, reigned from 1868 to 1910. He continued his father’s practice of granting concessions to the West to maintain Siam’s independence, losing large chunks of Laotian and Cambodian territory to the French and various bits of Malaysia to the British. He further reformed the monarchy and the government in general, including abolishing slavery, introducing a modern school system, constructing railways and telegraph systems, and establishing a new law court and judiciary."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_19", "拉玛四世的儿子拉玛五世于1868年至1910年在位。他延续了他父亲的做法，向西方国家让步，以保持暹罗的独立，将老挝和柬埔寨的大片领土输给了法国，并将马来西亚的各个地方输给了英国。他进一步改革了君主制和政府，包括废除奴隶制，引进现代学校制度，修建铁路和电报系统，并建立了新的法院和司法机构。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_20", "King Rama V’s two successors, the aptly-named Rama VI (ruled 1910-1925) and Rama VII (ruled 1925-1935), continued the modernization of Siam. In 1917 Rama VI opened the first university in Thailand. In that year he also entered World War I on the side of the Allies. He was able after the war to convince the victors to give up their special concessions in Siam, regaining for the first time in seventy-five years full independence for his country. However, Rama VI’s reforms and wars were extremely expensive and necessitated reductions in government spending which caused deep resentment from the people. The discontent continued into his successor’s reign, and it was exacerbated by the Great Depression."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_20", "拉玛五世的两个继任者，名字恰如其分的拉玛六世（1910-1925年在位）和拉玛七世（1925-1935年在位），继续推进暹罗的现代化进程。1917年，拉玛六世开设了泰国的第一所大学。在这一年，他还站在同盟国一边参加了第一次世界大战。他在战后说服了战胜国放弃在暹罗的特殊优惠政策，使他的国家在75年中第一次获得了完全独立。然而，拉玛六世的改革和战争耗资巨大，必须削减政府开支，这引起了人民的强烈不满。这种不满情绪一直持续到他的继任者的统治时期，并因大萧条而加剧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_21", "In 1932 a group of students under a lawyer named 'Pridi Phanomyong' and supported by the Siamese military staged a bloodless coup, compelling the king to agree to rule under a constitution and to accept the formation of a National Assembly. In 1933 members of the royal family attempted unsuccessfully to stage a counter-coup, and King Rama VII was forced to leave the country, abdicating in 1935. A regency council was appointed to act until the very young Prince Ananda Mahidol came of age."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_21", "1932年，一群学生在一位名叫 “銮巴立”的律师的领导下，在暹罗军方的支持下，发动了一场不流血的政变，迫使国王同意根据宪法进行统治并接受国民议会的成立。1933年，王室成员试图发动反政变，但没有成功，拉玛七世国王被迫离开该国，于1935年退位。一个摄政委员会被任命为摄政委员会，直到非常年轻的拉玛八世王子成年。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_22", "In truth, however, the military was now running the country. In 1938 a field marshal (and one of the co-conspirators of the ’32 coup that toppled Rama VII) became military dictator. Dictator Phibun Songkhram changed the name of the country to Thailand, encouraged Thai nationalism as well as anti-Chinese and pro-Japanese sentiment. In 1940, following the conquest of France by Germany, he invaded and captured French territory in Laos and Cambodia."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_22", "然而，事实上，军队现在正在管理这个国家。1938年，一位元帅（也是推翻拉玛七世的32年政变的同谋之一）成为军事独裁者。独裁者銮披汶·颂堪将国家名称改为泰国，鼓励泰国民族主义以及反华和亲日情绪。1940年，在德国征服法国后，他入侵并占领了老挝和柬埔寨的法国领土。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_23", "Late in 1941, following the attack on Pearl Harbor, Japanese troops marched into Thailand and requested right of passage through the country to facilitate their attack on Singapore, which was held by Great Britain. The Thai forces put up minimal symbolic resistance and then were ordered to lay down their arms. In 1942 Thailand signed an Alliance with Japan and declared war on Britain and the US. Resistance groups formed in the country and overseas, attacking the Japanese and the collaborating Thai government. In July 1944 Phibun was forced to resign, and the dictatorship collapsed following Japan’s surrender in 1945."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_23", "1941年末，在偷袭珍珠港之后，日本军队开进泰国，要求获得通过该国的权利，以方便他们进攻由英国控制的新加坡。泰国军队进行了最低限度的象征性抵抗，然后被命令放下武器。1942年，泰国与日本签订了联盟，并向英国和美国宣战。在国内和海外形成了抵抗组织，攻击日本人和合作的泰国政府。1944年7月，披汶被迫辞职，1945年日本投降后，独裁政权瓦解。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_24", "Thailand got off relatively lightly following World War II. It had to return the territories it had snarfed up from the French, but generally it suffered no other penalties. It did suffer from a great deal of internal strife, however. In 1946 the king was found dead of a gunshot wound. The current leader of the government was blamed for the king’s death and forced into exile, the proto-fascist Dictator Phibun Songkhram returning to power."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_24", "二战后，泰国得到了相对宽松的待遇。它不得不归还它从法国人那里抢来的领土，但总体上没有受到其他惩罚。然而，它确实遭受了大量的内部纷争。1946年，国王被发现死于枪伤。现任政府领导人被指责为国王的死因，并被迫流亡，原法西斯独裁者銮披汶颂堪重新上台。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_25", "In the Cold War years the United States funneled huge sums of money into Thailand, most of which was taken by the military and the dictatorship. A majority of the country’s industry was owned by the dictator and his cronies, and in 1957 the military staged another coup, placing yet another field marshal, Sarit Thanarat, in charge."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_25", "在冷战时期，美国向泰国输送了大量的资金，其中大部分被军方和独裁者拿走。国家的大部分工业由独裁者和他的亲信拥有，1957年，军方再次发动政变，由另一位元帅沙立·他那叻负责。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_26", "Thanarat ruled for five years. While maintaining total control over the government and military, he implemented economic reforms that spread the wealth among the growing Thai middle class, earning a good deal of popular support for doing so. The US gave him even more money, which he used to support the military, but also to improve the Thai infrastructure. Thanarat also gave support to the monarchy, which by then had no political power, but which once again became a powerful symbol of Thai nationalism. A popular leader during his life, after his death Thanarat’s popularity waned a good deal when it was discovered how much of Thailand’s money he had stolen and hidden away."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_26", "他那叻统治了五年。在保持对政府和军队的完全控制的同时，他实施了经济改革，将财富分散给日益壮大的泰国中产阶级，并为此赢得了大量的民众支持。美国给了他更多的钱，他用这些钱来支持军队，也用来改善泰国的基础设施。他那叻还支持君主制，当时君主制已经没有政治权力，但它再次成为泰国民族主义的有力象征。他那叻生前是一位受欢迎的领导人，但在他死后，当人们发现他偷了多少泰国的钱并把它们藏起来时，他的受欢迎程度就大大降低了。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_27", "Thanarat’s successors continued to receive huge amounts of American money, and in return they supported the American adventure in Vietnam. By the end of the 1960s more than 10,000 Thai troops were serving in Vietnam, and thousands of American soldiers were stationed in Thailand, which provided an important base for the US Air Force. Popular discontent for the war and the government grew, and in 1973 a student-led revolt drove the current leaders into exile."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_27", "他那叻的继任者继续收到大量的美国资金，作为回报，他们支持美国在越南的冒险。到20世纪60年代末，超过1万名泰国军队在越南服役，数千名美国士兵驻扎在泰国，泰国是美国空军的一个重要基地。民众对战争和政府的不满与日俱增，1973年，一场由学生领导的叛乱将现任领导人赶到了国外。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_28", "Thailand enjoyed a brief period of parliamentary democracy, but in 1976 the military staged yet another coup, this time with the support of the monarchy. This in turn drove many disaffected Thais into the jungles, swelling the ranks of the insurgent Communist Party of Thailand. In 1980 the military ousted the right-wing government they had just installed and replaced it with a dictator with more democratic leanings. For the next eight years the military shared power with parliament, mediated by the king, and in 1988 an elected Prime Minister was put in power… for three years, when he was toppled by the military."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_28", "泰国曾有过一段短暂的议会民主时期，但在1976年，军方又发动了一次政变，这次是在君主制的支持下。这反过来又把许多心怀不满的泰国人赶进了丛林，使叛乱的泰国共产党的队伍不断壮大。1980年，军方推翻了他们刚刚建立的右翼政府，代之以一个具有更多民主倾向的独裁者。在接下来的八年里，军方在国王的调停下与议会分享权力，1988年，一位当选的总理开始执政......三年后，他被军方推翻。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_29", "In 1992 the military 'junta' held elections, which one of its own members won, much to nobody’s surprise. The public were dissatisfied with this outcome, staging massive protests, which were put down with bloody force. Eventually the king intervened, the current dictator resigned and a more democratic government was put into place. This lasted for eight years, until in 2006, increasing public dissatisfaction and government excesses led to… another military coup."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SIAM_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_29", "1992年，军政府举行了选举，它自己的一名成员赢得了选举，没有人感到惊讶。公众对这一结果感到不满，举行了大规模的抗议活动，这些抗议活动被血腥的武力镇压。最终，国王进行了干预，现任独裁者辞职，一个更加民主的政府被建立起来。这种情况持续了八年，直到2006年，越来越多的公众不满和政府的过度行为导致了......另一场军事政变。"),
("en_US", "LOC_LOADING_INFO_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG", "The people of Siam await your command, King Ramkhamhaeng. Cultivate your relationships with the states around you and allow trade to flow, then surely the best they have to offer will come to you. Rule them and your people like a father governs his children, and through their loyalty, Siam will flourish."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_LOADING_INFO_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG", "暹罗人民在等待你的命令，兰甘亨国王。培养你与周围国家的关系，允许贸易流动，那么他们财赋肯定使你富裕。像父亲管理孩子一样管理他们和你的人民，通过他们的忠诚，暹罗将蓬勃发展。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "My father was named Sri Indraditya, my mother was named Nang Sueng, and I am King Ramkhamhaeng. On behalf of all the people of Sukhothai, I bid you welcome to my kingdom."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "我的父亲叫父亲名为室利·因陀罗，母亲是苏昂，而我是兰甘亨国王。我代表素可泰的全体人民，欢迎你们来到我的王国。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_VISIT_RECIPIENT_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "We have a city nearby. Perhaps you’d be interested in joining me in some restful meditation? Then afterwards, I can show you around."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_VISIT_RECIPIENT_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "我们在附近有一个城市。也许你有兴趣和我一起做一些静心的冥想？之后，我可以带你参观。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NEAR_INITIATOR_POSITIVE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Thank you for your hospitality. I only hope I will be able to reciprocate."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NEAR_INITIATOR_POSITIVE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "谢谢你的热情款待。我希望我能够得到回报。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NO_MANS_INFO_EXCHANGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Tell me about your capital, and I will tell you of mine. It’s only good diplomacy"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NO_MANS_INFO_EXCHANGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "告诉我你的首都，我也会告诉你我的。这是良好的外交手段。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Fish in the water, rice in the fields. I’m pleased to see you care for your people’s happiness and well-being."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "水里有鱼，田里有稻。我很高兴看到你关心你的人民的幸福和教养。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "A ruler ought to be like a father to his people. Do not forget the duty you owe to those you rule."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "统治者应该像父亲一样对待人民。别忘记你对你人民的使命。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "We are a peaceful nation, but do not think we will shy away from battle!"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "虽然我们是爱好和平的国家，但是别以为我们羞于战争！"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "I do this for the well being of the world and of Siam. All will be happier when you are brought down!"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "我这样做是为了世界和暹罗的福祉。当你被打倒后，所有的人都会更快乐!"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_ACCEPT_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "My people welcome the end of this pointless conflict."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_ACCEPT_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "我的人民欢迎这场无意义的冲突的结束。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_REFUSE_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "My people demand this war continues. I cannot yet make peace."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_REFUSE_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "我的人民要求这场战争继续下去。我还不能实现和平。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "For the sake of our peoples, I beg you to end this war."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "为了我们的人民，我请求你结束这场战争。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Siam may fall today, but we have suffered defeats before, and we will ascend again."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "暹罗今天或许倒下了，但我们以前也遭受过失败，我们会再次崛起。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "You are a wise ruler who cares for his people. Siam is honored to extend to you a hand in friendship."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "您是一位关心人民的明智的统治者。暹罗很荣幸能向您伸出友谊之手。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Excellent, both our peoples will be happier for it!"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "很好，我们两国的人民都会因此而更加幸福！"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Unfortunate. But I’m certain you have your reasons."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "不幸。但我确信你有你的理由。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "I gladly accept, on behalf of my people."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "我代表人民荣幸地接受。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "I don’t believe this is the right time for us to make such a declaration."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "我不认为现在是我们发表这种声明的正确时机。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DELEGATION_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "A trade delegation should arrive shortly with some fine Sangkhalok ceramic ware. I’ve thrown in a few sweets for you in the jars. Enjoy!"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DELEGATION_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "一个贸易代表团很快就会带着一些精美的宋加洛陶器到达。我在罐子里给你放了一些糖果，请享用吧!"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Your delegation has been gratefully received. They are resting in the lakeside Sala enjoying the lotus blossoms as we speak."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "你们的代表团已被我们怀着感激地接待。就在我们说话的时候，他们正在湖边的亭阁里休息，享受观赏荷花的乐趣。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "No, thank you. My people already have plenty and to accept such gifts would be wasteful."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "不，谢谢你。我的人民已经有很多财富，接受这样的礼物将是无意义的。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "The wellbeing of my people belies your false words."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "你的虚伪之词掩盖不了我的人民的福祉。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "I have never seen such ignominious behavior. How can you think yourself fit to rule a nation? (Denounces You)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "我从未见过如此无耻的行为。你怎么能认为自己适合统治一个国家？(谴责你)"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Let us work together, to make the world a happier and more prosperous place. Please, join me in an alliance!"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "让我们一起努力，使世界更幸福、更繁荣。请加入我的联盟!"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_GREETING_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Welcome."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_GREETING_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "欢迎。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "This is not to the benefit of my people."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "这对我的人民来说是不利的。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Yes, I think the people of Siam will benefit from this."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "是的，我认为暹罗人民将从中受益。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "I beg you to allow my people access to your fine nation."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "我请求你允许我的人民进入你的美好国家。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "Siam is always open for the weary traveler. Your people are welcome."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "暹罗始终为疲惫的旅行者敞开大门。我们欢迎你的人民。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "For the safety of my people, I must unfortunately deny your request. I do hope you can understand."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "为了我的人民的安全，我必须不幸地拒绝你的请求。我很希望你能理解。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "I do hope your encroachment is but a misunderstanding? Please move your troops away."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_ANY", "I do hope your encroachment is but a misunderstanding? Please move your troops away."),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_QUOTE", "In the water there is fish and in the fields there is rice."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_QUOTE", "水里有鱼，田里有稻。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_TITLE", "Pho Khun Ramkhamhaeng"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_TITLE", "兰甘亨大帝"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_SUBTITLE", "Rama the Bold"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_SUBTITLE", "勇敢的拉玛"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_CAPSULE_BODY", "As in history, Siam is a center of diplomacy and commerce. Under Ramkhamhaeng, Siam’s strong economic base combined with its City-State tributaries will allow Siam to pursue any victory."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_CAPSULE_BODY", "和历史上一样，暹罗是一个外交和商业中心。在兰甘亨的领导下，暹罗强大的经济基础加上其城邦藩属，将使暹罗能够追求任何胜利。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_DETAILED_BODY", "Siam is an unrivaled diplomat, gaining an additional Envoy when completing any Civic that already provides them. The City-State friends they gain will provide useful yield boosts to Siam’s districts. To help aid with this, place districts next to a river to gain extra [ICON_Amenities] Amenities to aid with expansion. Siam’s Floating Markets will incentivise grabbing Luxury Resources as well, providing [ICON_Culture] Culture and [ICON_Gold] Gold when working them, so keep that in mind when founding your cities. Ramkhamhaeng augments this already very versatile mix of abilities, by providing more [ICON_Gold] Gold for pursuing [ICON_TechBoosted] Eurekas and [ICON_CivicBoosted] Inspirations. Essentially, build up a strong economic and diplomatic base, then leverage it for victory."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_DETAILED_BODY", "暹罗是一个无与伦比的外交家，当完成任何已经提供特使的公民时，会获得一个额外的特使。他们获得的城邦朋友将为暹罗的地区提供有用的收益提升。为了帮助实现这一目标，将地区放在河流旁边可以获得额外的 [ICON_Amenities] 宜居度以帮助扩张。暹罗的水上市场也会激励人们去攫取奢侈资源，在使用它们时提供 [ICON_Culture] 文化和 [ICON_Gold] 金币，所以在建立城市时要记住这点。兰甘亨通过提供更多的 [ICON_Gold] 金币来追求 [ICON_TechBoosted] 尤里卡和 [ICON_CivicBoosted] 鼓舞，增强了这个已经非常通用的能力组合。基本上，建立一个强大的经济和外交基础，然后利用它来取得胜利。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "In 1278, a prince named “Ramkhamhaeng” inherited the small and unimportant kingdom of Sukhothai. In twenty years, employing a brilliant combination of military genius and shrewd diplomacy, he expanded his country’s borders and influence to cover much of Southeast Asia."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "1278年，一位名叫“兰甘亨”的王子继承了小而不重要的素可泰王国。在二十年间，他运用军事天才和精明的外交手段的杰出组合，扩大了他的国家的边界和影响力，覆盖了东南亚的大部分地区。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "Not much is known about Ramkhamhaeng’s early life. His parents were King Sri Indraditya and Queen Sueang. He had two sisters and two older brothers, one of whom died early and the other, Ban Mueang, became king on their father’s death. Ramkhamhaeng was said to have studied under the poet wise-man Sukathanta. At 19 he served under his father during the latter’s attack on the city of Sukhothai, which was held by the Khmer. The success of this attack greatly expanded the king’s power, essentially establishing Sukhothai as an independent kingdom. Because of his heroic actions during the battle the prince was given the title 'Phra Ram Khamhaeng', or Rama the Bold. Upon the death of his father in 1257, his brother, the new king Ban Mueang, put Ramkhamhaeng in charge of the city of Si Satchanalai. Ban Mueang died twenty years later, and Ramkhamhaeng ascended to the throne."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "关于兰甘亨的早期生活，人们知之甚少。他的父母是室利·因陀罗国王和苏昂王后。他有两个姐姐和两个哥哥，其中一个很早就去世了，另一个叫班孟，在他们父亲去世后成为国王。据说兰甘亨曾在诗人智者苏卡坦塔的指导下学习。19岁时，他在他父亲的手下工作，当时他父亲正在攻打被高棉人占领的素可泰城。这次进攻的成功极大地扩大了国王的权力，基本上将素可泰建立为一个独立的王国。由于他在战斗中的英勇行为，王子被赋予了“Phra Ram Khamhaeng”的称号，即大胆的拉玛。1257年，他的父亲去世后，他的兄弟，新国王班孟，让兰甘亨负责西沙差那莱的事务。20年后，班孟去世，兰甘亨登上了王位。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "During his reign Ramkhamhaeng expanded his kingdom’s dominance west into Burma, east into Laos, and south down the Malay Peninsula. The king was a shrewd diplomat as well as a warlord; many territories joined his confederation voluntarily. Ramkhamhaeng did not seek to dominate Southeast Asia, rather he promoted trade and diplomatic alliances with surrounding kingdoms."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "兰甘亨在位期间，将其王国的统治权向西扩展到缅甸，向东扩展到老挝，向南扩展到马来半岛。这位国王是一位精明的外交家，也是一位军阀；许多地区自愿加入他的联盟。兰甘亨并不寻求统治东南亚，而是促进与周边王国的贸易和外交联盟。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "Regarded as a benevolent and wise ruler, one of his major achievements was the compilation of a system of writing and a new Thai alphabet which he adapted from the various forms of Khmer script that were previously used. The alphabet King Ramkhamhaeng the Great devised in 1283 is essentially the same as that which is used today in Thailand and he is sometimes referred to as the ‘Father of the Thai language’. He has also been credited as the most important figure in establishing Theravada Buddhism in Thailand although the extent of his role is disputed by some historians."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "他被认为是一位仁慈和明智的统治者，他的主要成就之一是编制了一套书写系统和新的泰语字母，它从以前使用的各种形式的高棉文字中改编而来。兰甘亨大帝在1283年设计的字母表与今天在泰国使用的字母表基本相同，他有时被称为“泰语之父”。他也被认为是在泰国建立上部座佛教的最重要人物，尽管一些历史学家对他的作用有争议。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "Ramkhamhaeng died in 1298. His extended empire, held together by his personal magnetism and brilliant international diplomacy, did not long survive his death, and the furthest provinces soon broke away. Sukhothai itself survived another century before it fell."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "兰甘亨于1298年去世。虽然他的个人魅力和出色的国际外交活动功勋卓著，但他的庞大帝国没有在他死后存活多久，最远的省份很快就分裂了。素可泰本身在灭亡前又存活了一个世纪。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "Ramkhamhaeng is viewed today as a great leader and the first to rule over a united Siam (later Thailand). It should be remembered however that almost all that we know about him comes from the stone inscription that he himself created. If he did have any major flaws, would he have carved them into the living rock for all of history to see? (Would any of today’s world leaders do so?) Still, there is plenty of independent evidence to show that he successfully created a great empire and his people prospered during his reign. And that’s a record that any leader could be proud of."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_RAMKHAMHAENG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "兰甘亨今天被认为是一位伟大的领袖，是第一个统治统一的暹罗（后来的泰国）的人。然而，应该记住，我们对他的了解几乎都来自于他自己创作的石刻。如果他确实有任何重大缺陷，他会把它们刻在活生生的石头上让所有的历史看到吗？(今天的世界领导人会这样做吗？）不过，还是有很多独立的证据表明，他成功地创建了一个伟大的帝国，他的人民在他的统治下繁荣昌盛。而这是一个任何领导人都可以引以为豪的记录。"),
("en_US", "LOC_UNIT_SIAMESE_EXPEDITIONARY_FORCES_NAME", "Siamese Expeditionary Forces"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_UNIT_SIAMESE_EXPEDITIONARY_FORCES_NAME", "暹罗欧洲志愿军");

-- Siam (Chulalongkorn)
insert or replace into LocalizedText (Language, Tag, Text) values
("en_US", "LOC_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_NAME", "Chulalongkorn"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_NAME", "朱拉隆功"),
("en_US", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_SUK_MONTHON_SYSTEM_NAME", "Monthon System"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_SUK_MONTHON_SYSTEM_NAME", "蒙通体系"),
("en_US", "LOC_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_NAME", "Damrong"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_NAME", "丹隆"),
("en_US", "LOC_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_TITLE", "The Mahatthai"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_TITLE", "摩诃泰"),
("en_US", "LOC_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_SHORT_TITLE", "Mahatthai"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_SHORT_TITLE", "摩诃泰"),
("en_US", "LOC_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_DESCRIPTION", "Chulalongkorn’s right-hand man; {LOC_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_NAME} doesn’t improve any one city or have any specific focus, but provides [ICON_Production] Production, [ICON_Food] Food, [ICON_Science] Science, and [ICON_Culture] Culture bonuses to all the cities in a region."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_DESCRIPTION", "朱拉隆功的得力助手；丹隆不改善任何一个城市或有任何特定的重点，但为一个地区的所有城市提供[ICON_Production] 生产力、[ICON_Food] 粮食、[ICON_Science] 科技和 [ICON_Culture] 文化的奖励。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "A son of King Mongkut by a lesser royal wife, Prince Damrong Rajanubhab was a younger half-brother of King Chulalongkorn. He was the founder of modern education and provincial administration and was Thailand’s leading intellectual of his generation. Damrong himself had only four years of formal education in short-lived palace Thai and English schools founded by King Chulalongkorn for his brothers in the early 1870s. Following this schooling he joined the Royal Pages’ Bodyguard Regiment to prepare for a military career. When he became head of the regiment in 1880, at the age of 18, he found that the sons of royalty and nobility passing through the pages’ corps were being ill-prepared for military and bureaucratic careers and so founded Suan Kulap (Rose Garden Palace) School in 1881. In 1885 an education department was created under Damrong’s control, which in 1887 was made a separate department of government and in 1892 a ministry."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "丹隆·拉差努帕亲王是蒙固国王的儿子，是朱拉隆功国王同父异母的兄弟。他是泰国现代教育和省级行政管理的创始人，是泰国同时代的重要知识分子。丹隆本人只在朱拉隆功国王于19世纪70年代初为他的兄弟们建立的短暂的宫廷泰语和英语学校接受了四年的正规教育。在这所学校学习之后，他加入了皇家侍卫团，为军事生涯做准备。1880年，当他18岁成为该团团长时，他发现通过侍从团的皇室和贵族子弟对军事和官僚职业的准备不足，因此在1881年成立了Suan Kulap（玫瑰园宫）学校。1885年，在丹隆的控制下成立了一个教育部门，1887年该部门成为政府的一个独立部门，1892年成为一个部。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "Damrong was slated to become the minister of education in 1892 but instead, because of his exceptional ability, was appointed Minister of the Interior (or “Minister of the Mahatthai” in Thai), the most powerful position in the bureaucracy. He modernized what had been a decentralized system of provincial administration by grouping almost 100 provinces into only 14 “circles,” each staffed by modern-educated young officers and royal commissioners, thus quickly ending provincial autonomy. Damrong’s officers collected taxes, controlled leasing for the extraction of natural resources, and introduced modern law and education."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "1892年，丹隆被任命为教育部长，但由于他能力出众，被升为为内政部长（泰语为“摩诃泰部长”），这是官僚机构中权力最大的职位。他将原本分散的省级行政系统现代化，将近100个省归为14个“圈”，每个圈都由受过现代教育的年轻官员和皇家专员组成，从而迅速结束了省级自治。丹隆的官员们征收税款，控制自然资源开采的租赁，并引入现代法律和教育。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "After being encouraged to resign by his young nephew King Vajiravudh in 1915, Damrong turned his energies to scholarship. He took a leading role in preserving and publishing the traditional texts of Thai literature and history, and he was one of the founders of the Siam Society and the National Library. Damrong went into exile in Pinang after the 1932 revolution. He was the author of more than 1,000 books and articles in various fields."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_SUK_DAMRONG_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "1915年，在他年轻的侄子瓦栖拉兀国王的鼓励下，丹隆将精力转向学术研究。他在保护和出版泰国文学和历史的传统文本方面发挥了主导作用，他也是暹罗协会和国家图书馆的创始人之一。1932年革命后，丹隆流亡到了槟城。他撰写了1000多本书籍和不同领域的文章。"),
("en_US", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_ROYAL_SURVEY_NAME", "Survey Department"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_ROYAL_SURVEY_NAME", "测量部门"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_ROYAL_SURVEY_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "The brainchild of Prince Damrong, King Chulalongkorn established the Thai Survey School in 1882, with initial recruits coming from the Royal Guards. A royal decree issued September 3, 1885, separated the surveyors from the royal bodyguard and created the Royal Survey Department. The department engaged in cadastral survey, which is the survey of specific land parcels to define ownership for land registration, and for equitable taxation. Land title deeds were issued using the Torrens title system. It was not until the year 1901 that the first–fruits of this survey were obtained."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_ROYAL_SURVEY_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "朱拉隆功国王在1882年建立了泰国测量学校，最初招募的人员来自皇家卫队，是达丹隆王子的倡议。1885年9月3日颁布的一项皇家法令将测量人员从皇家卫队中分离出来，并成立了皇家测量部。该部门从事地籍调查，即对特定地块的调查，以确定土地登记的所有权，并进行公平的税收。土地所有权证书是采用托伦斯产权制度颁发的。直到1901年，这项调查才取得了初步成果。"),
("en_US", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SANITARY_DISTRICTS_NAME", "Sanitary Districts"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SANITARY_DISTRICTS_NAME", "卫生区"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SANITARY_DISTRICTS_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "While the first Sukhaphiban, or “Sanitary District”, was first established in 1897, the majority of these were established in response to plague outbreaks in 1904 and 1906. Sukhaphiban were charged with maintaining public hygiene. The districts were administered by a sanitation committee, which consisted of “Kamnan” (“Tambon” or sub-district headmen), village headmen, and also local merchants. It was financed by a housing tax on local residents."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SANITARY_DISTRICTS_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "虽然第一个苏卡吡班，或称“卫生区”，最早成立于1897年，但大多数都是在1904年和1906年爆发鼠疫时建立的。苏卡吡班负责维护公共卫生。这些地区由卫生委员会管理，该委员会由 Kamnan总长官（Tambon小区或分区区长）、村长和当地商人组成。它的资金来自于对当地居民征收的住房税。"),
("en_US", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SUANKULARB_COLLEGE_NAME", "Suan Kulap College"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SUANKULARB_COLLEGE_NAME", "玫瑰园学院"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SUANKULARB_COLLEGE_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "Suan Kulap (or Suankularb) Wittayalai, was a College founded by Prince Damrong in 1881, specifically to educate civil servants. Suan Kulap is a college in the sense often used in the UK and other commonwealth countries, being the oldest public secondary school in the country (simply put, it’s a high school, not a university). Under the patronage and guidance of King Chulalongkorn the school grew quickly, and the number of students rapidly swelled to many hundreds. Suan Kulap alumni include eight Prime Ministers of Thailand, nine Supreme Court Chief Justices, five attorneys general, two Fortune Global 500 chief executives, scholars, as well as a number of prominent politicians and businessmen."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SUANKULARB_COLLEGE_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "玫瑰园学院，是由丹隆亲王在1881年建立的一所学院，专门教育公务员。玫瑰园学院是英国和其他英联邦国家经常使用的意义上的学院，是该国最古老的公立中学（简单地说，它是一所高中，而不是一所大学）。在朱拉隆功国王的赞助和指导下，学校发展迅速，学生人数迅速膨胀到数百人。玫瑰园学院的校友包括八位泰国总理、九位最高法院首席法官、五位总检察长、两位《财富》全球500强企业的首席执行官、学者，以及一些著名的政治家和商人。"),
("en_US", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_MONTHON_REFORMS_NAME", "Monthon Reforms"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_MONTHON_REFORMS_NAME", "蒙通改革"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_MONTHON_REFORMS_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "The establishment of the Monthon Thesaphiban system is perhaps the most significant act of Chulalongkorn's reign. Headed by Prince Damrong, the reforms transformed the country from a decentralized system of semi-independent tributary cities into a centralized nation-state in line with the nations of the West. The reforms merged almost 100 provinces into only 14 “Monthons” (literally “circles”), obliterating the power of local lords and even tributary kings, and forcing taxes into the central government’s purse, rather than those of the local lords. Such a major change did not occur without incident, and revolts sprang up in both the Lanna and Isan regions; though they were ultimately suppressed—rebels armed with only local weapons and holy water were no match for the government’s Gatling guns and cannons."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_MONTHON_REFORMS_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "蒙通体系的建立可能是朱拉隆功统治时期最重要的行为。在丹隆亲王的领导下，改革将国家从一个由半独立的城邦组成的分散系统转变为一个与西方国家一致的中央集权民族国家。改革将近100个省合并为14个“月”（字面意思是“圈”），取消了地方领主甚至是藩属国王的权力，并迫使税收进入中央政府的钱包，而不是地方领主的钱包。如此重大的变革并非没有发生过，兰纳和伊桑地区都出现了起义；尽管他们最终被镇压了——仅有当地武器和圣水的叛军无法与政府的加特林机枪和大炮相比。"),
("en_US", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SIAM_SOCIETY_NAME", "The Siam Society"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SIAM_SOCIETY_NAME", "暹罗学会"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SIAM_SOCIETY_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "The Siam Society (Under Royal Patronage) was founded in 1904 in cooperation with Thai and foreign scholars, with Prince Damrong as one of its founding members. The Society soon established a reputation as a learned society whose members included many of the most illustrious historians and archaeologists of that period. The Siam Society presents lectures by local and international experts in English and Thai; holds exhibitions of  books, arts and artefacts; hosts international conferences; is involved in cultural preservation; stages cultural and musical performances; publishes the Journal of the Siam Society, Natural History Bulletin of the Siam Society and scholarly books; owns and operates a library with an outstanding collection of rare books and palm-leaf manuscripts; and has an ethnological museum in a magnificent old teak house situated on its grounds."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_SIAM_SOCIETY_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "暹罗学会（在皇家赞助下）是在泰国和外国学者的合作下于1904年成立的，丹隆亲王是其创始成员之一。学会很快就建立了学识渊博的声誉，其成员包括许多当时最杰出的历史学家和考古学家。暹罗学会用英语和泰语举办当地和国际专家的讲座；举办书籍、艺术和手工艺品展览；主办国际会议；参与文化保护；举办文化和音乐表演；出版《暹罗学会杂志》、《暹罗学会自然历史公报》和学术书籍；拥有并经营一个图书馆，收藏了大量珍稀书籍和棕榈叶手稿；并在其院内一座宏伟的老柚木屋中设立了民族学博物馆。"),
("en_US", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_KHWAM_SIWILAI_NAME", "Khwam Siwilai"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_KHWAM_SIWILAI_NAME", "文明开化"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_KHWAM_SIWILAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "“Siwilai”, a Thai-ification of the word “Civilised”, was born in reaction to the encroachment of the West in Asia. Many amongst the royalty and nobility of Siam, understood that to avoid colonisation, the nation would have to demonstrate their right to rule by adapting to the model of the nation-state that was dominant in the West, as well as adapting certain cultural norms. By self-initialising the process of Westernisation, Siam was able to define for itself what it meant to be “Siwilai”. Siam adopted Western technologies, such as the railroad and the telegraph. It reformed its systems of administration (see the Monthon Reforms). It strengthened its cultural and national identity both at home and abroad, participating in numerous World’s Fairs starting with one in 1867 in Paris. Siam also managed to reject a number of Western cultural standards, such as Christianity (it clung to Theravada Buddhism), and monogamy (though Thailand would reject polygamy early in the 20th century)."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_PAGE_GOVERNOR_PROMOTION_SUK_DAMRONG_KHWAM_SIWILAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "“Siwilai”是“文明”一词的泰语化，它的诞生是对西方在亚洲的侵占的反应。暹罗王室和贵族中的许多人明白，为了避免殖民化，国家必须通过适应在西方占主导地位的民族国家的模式，以及适应某些文化规范来证明他们的统治权。通过自我启动西化进程，暹罗能够为自己定义“暹罗”的含义。暹罗采用了西方技术，如铁路和电报。它改革了其行政系统（见蒙通改革）。它加强了其在国内和国外的文化和民族特性，从1867年在巴黎举行的世界博览会开始，参加了许多世界博览会。暹罗还设法拒绝了一些西方文化标准，如基督教（它坚持小乘佛教）和一夫一妻制（后来泰国在20世纪初取消了一夫多妻制）。"),
("en_US", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_PHRA_PIYA_MAHARAT_NAME", "Phra Piya Maharat"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_PHRA_PIYA_MAHARAT_NAME", "朱拉隆功大帝"),
("en_US", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_PHRA_PIYA_MAHARAT_DESCRIPTION", "Respects civilizations whose home contintinent is different from his own. Hates colonialists from other continents who settle cities on his home continent."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_PHRA_PIYA_MAHARAT_DESCRIPTION", "尊重那些与自己的家乡不同的文明。憎恨来自其他大陆的殖民者在他的家乡大陆上建立城市。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_REASON_ANY", "(You are from a different continent.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_REASON_ANY", "（你来自其他大陆）"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_PHRA_PIYA_MAHARAT_FOREIGNER", "Chulalongkorn respects civilizations from other continents"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_PHRA_PIYA_MAHARAT_FOREIGNER", "朱拉隆功尊重其他大陆的文明"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_REASON_ANY", "(You are colonsing his home continent.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_REASON_ANY", "（你殖民了他的家乡大陆）"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_PHRA_PIYA_MAHARAT_COLONISER", "Chulalongkorn hates that you are encroaching on his home continent"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_PHRA_PIYA_MAHARAT_COLONISER", "朱拉隆功痛恨你们侵占他的家园大陆"),
("en_US", "LOC_LOADING_INFO_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN", "Beloved King Chulalongkorn, your enlightened rule will bring Siam to prosperity. Care not for far away lands, for there are far greater rewards to be found at home. Nurture and defend your nation from those who would dare threaten it, and surely Siam will emerge the envy of the world."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_LOADING_INFO_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN", "敬爱的朱拉隆功国王，您的开明统治将使暹罗走向繁荣。不要关心遥远的土地，因为在国内可以找到更大的回报。培养和保卫你的国家，使其不受那些人的威胁，暹罗肯定会成为世界称羡的对象。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "That is truly a shame."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "这真是一种耻辱。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "It is done."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "已经完成了。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Though I am reluctant to entangle Siam in foreign issues, I think friendship between our nations would be beneficial. What say you?"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "虽然我不愿意在外交事务纠缠暹罗，但我认为我们国家之间的友谊会有好处。你怎么说？"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "I do not believe such an agreement is in Siam's best interest."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我认为这样的协议不符合暹罗的最佳利益。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Agreed, may both our nations grow stronger for it."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "同一，这将使我们两国都更强大。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Your very existence threatens our sovereignty. You must be stopped."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "你们的存在威胁着我们的主权。你必须被阻止。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "You are a fool! We will do our utmost to ensure Siam's survival."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "你真是个傻瓜！而我们将尽最大努力确保暹罗的生存。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Siam has not fallen, it has merely faltered, and we will one day return triumphant!"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "暹罗并没有完全沦陷，它只是暂时被挫败了。我们总有一天会凯旋而归！"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Siam has not fallen, it has merely faltered, and we will one day return triumphant!"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "暹罗并没有完全沦陷，它只是暂时被挫败了。我们总有一天会凯旋而归！"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DELEGATION_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "We have sent a delegation with the best silk and ivory Siam has to offer. Please treat them well."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DELEGATION_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我们的贸易使团带着我们所能提供的最好的丝绸和象牙。请善待他们。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "We politely refuse your delegation."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我们礼貌地拒绝您的代表团。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "We have received your trade delegation and you may rest assured that we will treat them with the dignity they deserve."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我们已经收到你们的贸易代表团，你们可以放心，我们授予他们应得的荣誉款待。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "The world now knows how Siam regards you. You are not to be trusted. (Denounces You)."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "现在全世界都知道暹罗是如何看待你的。你是不值得信任的。(谴责你）。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Siam stands firm in the face of your threats. You will regret this insult."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "面对你们的威胁，暹罗立场坚定。你会为这种侮辱感到后悔的。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "I am Chulalongkorn, King of Siam, and I offer you my warmest greetings. If you treat Siam with respect, our nations will get along spendidly."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我是暹罗国王朱拉隆功，我向你们表示最热烈的问候。如果你尊重暹罗，我们两国将会相处得很愉快。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_VISIT_RECIPIENT_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "We have a city nearby. Would you like to visit? I just commissioned a number of oil paintings for my residence there."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_VISIT_RECIPIENT_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我们附近有一个城市。你想去看看吗？我刚刚为我在那里的住所委托创作了一些油画作品。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NEAR_INITIATOR_POSITIVE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Thank you for your hospitality, we accept."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NEAR_INITIATOR_POSITIVE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "谢谢你的热情款待，我们接受。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NO_MANS_INFO_EXCHANGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "My capital? It's named Krungthep Mahanakhon Amonrattanakosin Mahintharayutthaya Mahadilokphop… actually nevermind, tell me of your capital."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NO_MANS_INFO_EXCHANGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我的首都？它叫天使之城，宏伟之城，永恒的宝石之城，永不可摧的因陀罗之城......事实上，算了，告诉我你的首都。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_GREETING_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Welcome."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_GREETING_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "欢迎"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Your encroachment on my continent is not at all welcome. Colonialism is a plague upon the earth."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "你们对我的大陆的侵占一点也不受欢迎。殖民主义是地球上的一种瘟疫。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Different lands have different ideas and values. We have much to learn from one another."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "不同的土地有不同的想法和价值观。我们有很多东西可以相互学习。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Would you like to form an alliance?"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "你希望结成一个同盟吗？"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "{LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY}"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", ""),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "{LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY}"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", ""),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_ACCEPT_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "I accept your terms for peace."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_ACCEPT_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我接受你的和平要求。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_REFUSE_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "No. I cannot accept."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_REFUSE_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "不，我不接受。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "I do not want to be remembered as a warmonger. Let us put aside our differences."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我不想作为一个战争犯被人记住。让我们把我们的分歧放在一边。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Very well, I hereby grant you permission to pass through my lands."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "很好，我在此允许你通过我的土地。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "We are not interested at this time."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我们目前没有兴趣。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Will you allow our units to cross through your territory?"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "你会允许我们的部队穿越你的领土吗？"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "I can only assume this show of force was undertaken by mistake. Should I expect a careful withdrawal from our borders momentarily?"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我只能假设这次的武力展示是错误的。我是否应该期待他们马上从我们的边界小心翼翼地撤离？"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_NEGATIVE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "Your armies are an insult to Siamese sovereignty. Move them at once!"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_NEGATIVE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "你的军队是对暹罗主权的一种侮辱。马上把他们赶走!"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_POSITIVE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "We meant no disrespect. Our forces will relinquish their position immediately."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_POSITIVE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_ANY", "我们没有不尊重的意思。我们的部队将立即放弃他们的位置。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_QUOTE", "I made a resolution that I shalt do my level best, my utmost to preserve the sovereignty of Siam with its independence and wealth intact."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_QUOTE", "我下决心尽我最大的努力，尽力维护暹罗的主权，保持其独立和财富的完整。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_TITLE", "Chulalongkorn"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_TITLE", "朱拉隆功"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_SUBTITLE", "Phra Bat Somdet Phra Poraminthra Maha Chulalongkorn Phra Chunla Chom Klao Chao Yu Hua"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_SUBTITLE", "受敬爱的朱拉隆功大帝"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_CAPSULE_BODY", "As in history, Siam is a center of diplomacy and commerce. Chulalongkorn gives Siam strong domestic bonuses that encourage them to aim to develop their home continent and strive for industrialization."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_CAPSULE_BODY", "和历史上一样，暹罗是一个外交和商业中心。朱拉隆功给了暹罗强大的国内红利，鼓励他们以发展本国大陆为目标，努力实现工业化。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_DETAILED_BODY", "Siam is an unrivaled diplomat, gaining an additional Envoy when completing any Civic that already provides them. The City-State friends they gain will provide useful yield boosts to Siam's districts. To help aid with this, place districts next to a river to gain extra [ICON_Amenities] Amenities to aid with expansion. Siam's Floating Markets will incentivise grabbing Luxury Resources as well, providing [ICON_Culture] Culture and [ICON_Gold] Gold when working them, so keep that in mind when founding your cities. Chulalongkorn's bonuses will aid you in developing your home continent: cities founded there will recieve a small boost to get them up and running. After researching Industrialization however, these bonuses are tripled, making these bonuses much more potent. It thus becomes key to ensure that as much of your continent is under Siam's jurisdiction as possible."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_DETAILED_BODY", "暹罗是一个无与伦比的外交文明，当完成任何已经提供使者的市政时，会获得一个额外的使者。他们获得的城邦盟友将为暹罗的地区提供有用的收益。为了对此有所帮助，将区域放在河流旁边可以获得额外的 [ICON_Amenities] 宜居度以帮助扩张。暹罗的水上市场也会激励人们去攫取奢侈资源，在使用它们时提供 [ICON_Culture] 文化和 [ICON_Gold] 金币，所以在建立城市时要记住这点。朱拉隆功的加成将帮助你发展你的家乡大陆。因此，确保你的大陆尽可能多地在暹罗的管辖之下成为关键。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "Phra Bat Somdet Phra Poraminthra Maha Chulalongkorn Phra Chunla Chom Klao Chao Yu Hua, or Rama V, or as we will refer to him henceforth, Chulalongkorn, was the fifth monarch of Siam under the House of Chakri. His reign was characterized by the modernization of Siam, governmental and social reforms, and territorial concessions to the British and French. As Siam was threatened by Western expansionism, Chulalongkorn, through his policies and acts, managed to save Siam from colonisation. All his reforms were dedicated to ensuring Siam's survival in the face of Western colonialism, so that Chulalongkorn earned the epithet Phra Piya Maharat: the Great Beloved King."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "帕拔颂德·帕尊拉宗·浩昭育华，即拉玛五世，或者称之为朱拉隆功，是暹罗却克里王朝的第五任君主。他统治时期的特点是暹罗的现代化、政府和社会改革以及对英国和法国的领土让步。由于暹罗受到西方殖民主义的威胁，朱拉隆功通过他的政策和行为，设法使暹罗免于殖民化。他的所有改革都致力于确保暹罗在西方殖民主义面前的生存，因此朱拉隆功赢得了伟大的受敬爱的国王称号。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "Born September 20, 1853, King Rama V was to inherit the throne from his father, King Monkut (Rama IV), in 1868 at the tender age of 15. Because he was still a child, Thailand was governed by regency for the first five years of his reign and the boy King took advantage of the time to travel the world. His father had been one of Siam's most educated monarchs, recognizing the need for education and also the importance of the western world, yet understanding fully the threat of colonization. Wisely, he had instilled these principles in his son who was an apt student. During those first five years, King Chulalongkorn visited most of the major western powers, learning about their cultures, traditions, political organization and technology while in neighboring countries he spent time making political friends, realizing the need for allies in the fight to prevent colonization."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "拉玛五世生于1853年9月20日，1868年从他的父亲蒙固国王（拉玛四世）手中继承王位，当时他年仅15岁。由于他还是个孩子，在他执政的前五年，泰国由摄政王管理，这位小国王利用这段时间周游世界。他的父亲是暹罗受教育程度最高的君主之一，认识到教育的必要性和西方世界的重要性，但也充分了解殖民化的威胁。他明智地将这些原则灌输给了他的儿子，而他的儿子是个聪明的学生。在最初的五年里，朱拉隆功国王访问了大多数西方大国，了解他们的文化、传统、政治组织和技术，而在邻国，他花时间结交政治朋友，意识到在反对殖民的斗争中需要盟友。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "With the support of his brothers and young friends, the King began, in 1873, to attack the injustices of the old order and the power of his political rivals by attempting to impose centralized budgeting and accounting, streamlining a judicial system beset by delays and corruption, and inaugurating consultative legislative councils dominated by his young friends. These actions, accompanied by a decline in Wichaichan's prospects, brought on the 'Front Palace Crisis' of early 1875, when Wichaichan fled to the British consulate and demanded protection; had it been granted, Thailand would have become an Anglo-French protectorate in all but name. Britain and France, by refusing to support their consuls, treated the matter as an internal quarrel, and Chulalongkorn was able to bring about a resolution of the crisis. Peace, however, was bought at a high price, for the King's supporters were disbanded, the councils ceased to meet, and no further reforms were undertaken for a decade."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "在他的兄弟和年轻朋友的支持下，国王于1873年开始抨击旧秩序的不公正和他的政治对手的权力，试图实行中央预算和会计，精简受拖延和腐败困扰的司法系统，并成立了由他的年轻朋友主导的协商立法委员会。这些行动伴随着威猜猜的前景下滑，引发了1875年初的“前宫危机”，当时威猜猜逃到英国领事馆，要求得到保护；如果得到保护，泰国将成为名副其实的英法保护国。英国和法国拒绝支持其领事，将此事视为内部争吵，朱拉隆功得以解决危机。然而，和平是以高昂的代价换来的，因为国王的支持者被解散了，议会不再开会，而且在十年内没有进行进一步的改革。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "One of the most notable reforms that occured during his reign was the centralisation of Siam. The six ministries of traditional Thai government had been omnicompetent, each with its own tax collections, law courts, provinces to administer, and rights to unsupervised expenditure; and they tended to be dominated by the minister of the North (mahatthai) and the minister of the South (kalahom), whom the King had been almost powerless to control. The new system, introduced on April 1, 1892, had 12 functionally defined ministries responsible to the King. Central to the reform program was the work of the ministry of interior, directed from 1892 by Prince Damrong Rajanubhab. By grouping almost 100 provinces into just 14 'Monthon', Damrong was able to make effective use of a very small body of educated young men in rapidly strengthening Bangkok's control over hitherto semiautonomous provinces. As a result, state revenues doubled within 7 years, and the new administrative structure brought the rule of law, public works, and elementary public education to the most distant provinces by the turn of the century. Chulalongkorn's son Prince Rabi was appointed as minister of justice in 1896, and all Thai law was recodified along European lines by the end of the reign, and a centralized modern judicial system was introduced. Railway construction, financed until 1904 entirely out of current revenues, rapidly linked the country together as never before. The King took great care in choosing the men for these tasks and followed daily the progress of the work. He encouraged and supported the most able of them and gave them a free hand, while ever goading and criticizing the less decisive and mediocre."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "他在位期间进行的最引人注目的改革之一是暹罗的中央集权。传统泰国政府的六个部都是无所不能的，每个部都有自己的税收、法院、管理的省份和不受监督的支出权；他们往往被北方部长（mahatthai）和南方部长（kalahom）所控制，国王几乎无力控制他们。1892年4月1日实行的新制度有12个职能明确的部，对国王负责。改革计划的核心是内政部的工作，从1892年起由丹隆亲王领导。通过将近100个省分成14个“月”，丹隆能够有效地利用一小批受过教育的年轻人，迅速加强曼谷对迄今半自治省的控制。结果，国家收入在7年内翻了一番，新的行政结构在世纪之交将法治、公共工程和初级公共教育带到了最遥远的省份。朱拉隆功的儿子拉比王子在1896年被任命为司法部长，在统治末期，所有的泰国法律都按照欧洲的方式重新编纂，并引入了一个集中的现代司法系统。直到1904年，铁路建设的资金完全来自于政府收入，它以前所未有的速度将国家联系在一起。国王在选择执行这些任务的人员时非常谨慎，并每天跟踪工作的进展。他鼓励并支持他们中最有能力的人，给他们自由发挥的空间，而对那些不那么果断和平庸的人则不断进行劝说和批评。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "Until the 1880s Chulalongkorn generally could assume that he had the goodwill of the Western powers and counted on British support for Thai independence and upon the skillful diplomacy of Prince Devawongse, whose appointment as foreign minister in 1886 marked the resumption of reform. From the mid-1880s, however, French ambitions in Indochina began to clash with Thai rights of suzerainty over Laos. The Thai were powerless to halt the demands which escalated into the Franco-Thai War of 1893 and ended with French gunboats forcing their way up the Chaophraya River to Bangkok to demand the cession to France of the east bank of the Mekong River and the payment of a large indemnity. Britain, counted on to support the Thai, refused to intervene, and Laos was ceded to France."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "在19世纪80年代之前，朱拉隆功一般可以认为他拥有西方国家的善意，并指望英国对泰国独立的支持和德沃旺乔亲王娴熟的外交技巧，他在1886年被任命为外交部长标志着改革的恢复。然而，从19世纪80年代中期开始，法国在印度支那的野心开始与泰国对老挝的宗主国权利发生冲突。泰国人无力阻止这些要求，这些要求升级为1893年的法泰战争，最后法国炮艇强行沿湄公河进入曼谷，要求将湄公河东岸割让给法国并支付巨额赔偿金。被指望支持泰国的英国拒绝干预，老挝被割让给了法国。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "Chulalongkorn was disheartened and went into an almost year-long period of illness and depression. Once recovered, he began to take initiatives and responsibility he had earlier been more willing to share with his brothers. The Anglo-French Declaration of 1896 guaranteed the integrity of central Siam but left the northeast threatened by France and the south by Britain. Chulalongkorn's European tour of 1897 was, among other things, an attempt to secure new European interest in Thailand's continued independence, especially on the part of Russia and Germany. Whether the tour achieved this object or not, his reception by the European monarchs as an equal did give Chulalongkorn a new self-confidence and a realization that modernization did not necessarily mean Westernization: 'We must try to imitate what is good elsewhere, and at the same time not only to keep but to develop what is good and worthy of respect in our own national character and institutions', he declared upon his return."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "朱拉隆功心灰意冷，进入了一个几乎长达一年的疾病和抑郁期。一旦康复，他开始主动，承担起他先前更愿意与兄弟们分享的责任。1896年的《英法宣言》保证了暹罗中部的完整性，但使东北部受到法国的威胁，南部受到英国的威胁。朱拉隆功1897年的欧洲之行，除其他事项外，还试图确保欧洲对泰国继续独立的兴趣，特别是俄罗斯和德国方面。无论这次旅行是否达到了这个目的，欧洲君主对他的平等接待确实给朱拉隆功带来了新的自信，并认识到现代化并不一定意味着西方化。他在回国后宣称：“我们必须努力模仿其他地方的好东西，同时不仅要保持而且要发展我们自己民族性格和制度中的好东西，值得尊重。”"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "During the remainder of Chulalongkorn's reign rapid progress was made toward the resolution of Thailand's most serious problems in the field of foreign affairs. Small areas of Laos on the western bank of the Mekong and the western provinces of Cambodia were ceded to France in 1904 and 1907, and in return the Thai regained legal jurisdiction over French Asian subjects in Thailand. The cession to Britain of the four Malayan states of Kelantan, Trengganu, Kedah, and Perlis in 1909 brought Thailand similar legal concessions (although the abolition of extraterritoriality was still several decades away) and capital for the extension of the railways toward Singapore. Most of all, by the end of his reign the King could feel that his country's independence at last was secure."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "在朱拉隆功统治的剩余时间里，泰国在解决外交事务方面最严重的问题方面取得了快速进展。1904年和1907年，老挝在湄公河西岸的小部分地区和柬埔寨西部省份被割让给法国，作为回报，泰国人重新获得了对泰国境内法属亚洲人的法律管辖权。1909年，马来亚的吉兰丹、丁加奴、吉打和玻璃市四个州割让给英国，为泰国带来了类似的法律优惠（尽管废除治外法权仍需数十年时间），并为向新加坡延伸铁路提供了资金。最重要的是，在他的统治结束时，国王可以感觉到他的国家的独立终于得到了保障。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_8", "Chulalongkorn is perhaps best known in modern Thailand for his abolition of Siamese slavery. He associated the abolition of slavery in the United States with the bloodshed of the American Civil War. Chulalongkorn, to prevent such a bloodbath in Siam, provided several steps towards the abolition of slavery, not an extreme turning point from servitude to total freedom. Traditionally, Siamese slavery functioned differently from western slavery. Those who found themselves unable to live on their own sold themselves into slavery by rich noblemen. Likewise, when a debt was defaulted, the borrower would become a slave of the lender. If the debt was redeemed, the slave regained freedom. However, those whose parents were household slaves were bound to be slaves forever because their redemption price was extremely high. Because of economic conditions, people sold themselves into slavery in great numbers and in turn they produced a large number of household slaves. In 1867 they accounted for one-third of Siamese population. In 1874, Chulalongkorn enacted a law that lowered the redemption price of household slaves born in 1867 (his ascension year) and freed all of them when they had reached 21. The newly-freed slaves would have time to settle themselves as farmers or merchants so they would not become unemployed. In 1905, the Slave Abolition Act ended Siamese slavery in all forms."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_8", "朱拉隆功在现代泰国最有名的也许是他废除了暹罗奴隶制。他将美国废除奴隶制与美国内战中的流血事件联系起来。朱拉隆功为了防止在暹罗发生这样的流血事件，为废除奴隶制提供了几个步骤，而不是一个从奴役到完全自由的极端转折点。传统上，暹罗奴隶制的运作方式与西方奴隶制不同。那些发现自己无法独立生活的人把自己卖给富有的贵族做奴隶。同样，当债务被拖欠时，借款人将成为贷款人的奴隶。如果债务被赎回，奴隶就会重新获得自由。然而，那些父母是家庭奴隶的人注定要永远成为奴隶，因为他们的赎回价格非常高。由于经济条件的原因，人们大量出卖自己成为奴隶，反过来又产生了大量的家庭奴隶。1867年，他们占了暹罗人口的三分之一。1874年，朱拉隆功颁布了一项法律，降低了1867年（他的登基年）出生的家庭奴隶的赎回价格，并在他们年满21岁时全部释放。新获得自由的奴隶将有时间以农民或商人的身份安顿自己，这样他们就不会失业了。1905年，《废除奴隶法》结束了所有形式的暹罗奴隶制。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_9", "Especially in the 1880s, he was fond of traveling incognito and would wander the slums and streets of Bangkok at night clad as a peasant. He once stopped a royal procession to join, unannounced, a peasant wedding; and his numerous travel diaries are filled with recorded conversations with peasant farmers who told him local folklore or complained about local conditions. He was a man of broad interests, and his zeal for change did not diminish his appreciation of his country's traditions."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_9", "特别是在19世纪80年代，他喜欢隐姓埋名地旅行，晚上会扮成农民在曼谷的贫民窟和街道上徘徊。他曾经拦住一支皇家队伍，不经意间参加了一场农民的婚礼；他的大量旅行日记中充满了与农民的对话记录，这些农民告诉他当地的民间传说或抱怨当地的情况。他是一个兴趣广泛的人，他对变革的热忱并没有削弱他对自己国家传统的欣赏。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_10", "After one of the longest reigns in Thai history, he died on Oct. 23, 1910. During his 42-year reign, King Chulalongkorn succeeded in establishing a government based on the western system, which ultimately paved the way for the present democracy. He reformed the rule of law, established a proper judicial system and introduced compulsory military service, improving the country's national defense. He introduced the Baht (still in use today) as the official currency and made taxes directly payable to the government, cutting out the corrupt middlemen. King Chulalongkorn also set up Siam's first hospital based on western medical practices, the first medical school and a nationwide education system. For his role in ensuring the continued sovereignty and for his modernization of Siam, Chulalongkorn remains to this day, one of the most highly revered monarchs in Thai history."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_CHULALONGKORN_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_10", "在经历了泰国历史上最长的统治之一后，他于1910年10月23日去世。在他42年的统治期间，朱拉隆功国王成功地建立了一个基于西方制度的政府，这最终为现在的民主制度铺平了道路。他改革了法治，建立了适当的司法系统，并实行了义务兵役制，提高了国家的国防水平。他引入了泰铢（至今仍在使用）作为官方货币，并将税收直接支付给政府，砍掉了腐败的中间商。朱拉隆功国王还建立了暹罗的第一家基于西方医学实践的医院、第一所医学院和一个全国性的教育系统。由于朱拉隆功在确保暹罗的持续主权和现代化方面发挥的作用，他至今仍是泰国历史上最受尊敬的君主之一。");

-- Siam (Narai)
insert or replace into LocalizedText (Language, Tag, Text) values
("en_US", "LOC_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_NAME", "Narai"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_NAME", "那莱"),
("en_US", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_SUK_SIAMOISES_NAME", "Les Ambassades Siamoises"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_SUK_SIAMOISES_NAME", "暹罗大使馆"),
("en_US", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_PHRAKHLANG_NAME", "Phrakhlang Ministry"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_PHRAKHLANG_NAME", "阿育陀耶财政部"),
("en_US", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_PHRAKHLANG_DESCRIPTION", "Likes civilizations with high Diplomatic Favor who are allied with him. Is slighted by civilizations who have many alliances, but are not allied with him."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_AGENDA_SUK_PHRAKHLANG_DESCRIPTION", "喜欢高外交支持并与其同盟的文明，厌恶有多个盟友却不与其同盟的文明。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_REASON_ANY", "(You are an ally with high Diplomatic Favor.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_REASON_ANY", "你是一位拥有高外交支持的盟友。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_PHRAKHLANG_ALLIED", "Narai is pleased to have such a diplomatic ally"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_PHRAKHLANG_ALLIED", "那赖很高兴拥有你这样的盟友。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_REASON_ANY", "(You have many allies, but aren't allied with him.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_REASON_ANY", "（你有很多盟友，却不和他结盟。）"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_PHRAKHLANG_NOT_ALLIED", "Narai is slighted he is not one of your many allies"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_SUK_PHRAKHLANG_NOT_ALLIED", "你有众多盟友，那莱不是其中之一。他倍感不满。"),
("en_US", "LOC_LOADING_INFO_LEADER_SUK_NARAI", "Let your reign be a peaceful one, King Narai, that Siam may blossom in tranquil prosperity. An open-mind will win you many friends, and with care, those friendship will become indestructible alliances. Through trade with them your nations will both flourish and Siam will want for naught; the crown jewel of the world."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_LOADING_INFO_LEADER_SUK_NARAI", "那莱国王，愿暹罗在您的治下繁荣安定。您的开明吸引了众多朋友。在您的关怀下，他们会成为您坚不可摧的盟友。与他们的互惠贸易会让暹罗成为世界王冠之珠宝、。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "You must be the foreigner who asked for an audience. I am Narai, King of Siam."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "你一定是请求觐见的外国人。我是那莱，暹罗的国王。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_VISIT_RECIPIENT_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "My astronomers are predicting a total solar eclipse, visible from one of my nearby cities. Perhaps you would join me for a viewing?"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_VISIT_RECIPIENT_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我手下的占星术士预测到一场月全食，在附近的城市可见。想要和我一起观赏吗？"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NEAR_INITIATOR_POSITIVE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Your generosity speaks well of you. Thank you."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NEAR_INITIATOR_POSITIVE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我十分感激你的宽宏大量。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NO_MANS_INFO_EXCHANGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "If we are to trade with one another we must know the location of one another’s capitals. Agreed?"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NO_MANS_INFO_EXCHANGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "如果我们想要开展贸易，就必须了解对方首都的位置，你同意吗？"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "I count it my great fortune to have such an ally as shrewd as you, my august friend."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我认为拥有你一样精明的盟友是我的荣幸，我的挚友。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Siam is a rich and bountiful land. You will regret having ignored us as a possible ally."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_EXIT_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "暹罗地大物博，你应为不与我们结盟感到遗憾。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "I could have given you much in friendship, but you insist on seizing it all by force. So be it. My subjects and friends will destroy your band of robbers."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我本来可以友善地给予你很多东西，你却坚持用武力抢夺。那就这样吧。我的附庸和盟友们会消灭你这帮强盗。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "We have tried diplomacy, and it has yielded no fruit. War remains our only choice."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我们尝试外交手段无果。战争是我们最后的选择。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_ACCEPT_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Siam tires of this war. Let us have peace between us."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_ACCEPT_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "暹罗厌倦了这场战争，让我们和平相处吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_REFUSE_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "I regret to say, my answer is no."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_REFUSE_DEAL_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我很遗憾地拒绝你的要求。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "The suffering of our subjects has gone on for long enough. Let us seek peace."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我们的属国痛苦不堪，让我们和平相处吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "I tried to do my best for Siam and her people. It seems I have failed. Please look after my people in my absence."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我为了暹罗和人民尽心竭力。我失败了。在我走后，请照顾好我的人民。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Our two nations would be stronger if we were to declare our willingness to work together."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "如果我们愿意合作的话，两个国家将共同富强。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Wonderful! Let this be the beginning of something greater."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "很好！这会将我们引向伟大之处。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "That truely is a shame. Perhaps next time."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "真遗憾，下次再议吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Yes! May we be forever tied by friendship and commerce."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "好！愿契约和友谊使我们不再分离。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "My nobles are not ready to agree to such a generous offer. Perhaps with more familiarity between us?"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我国的贵族对您的慷慨之举尚未准备好。也许在我们更加熟悉之后再议？"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DELEGATION_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "I send Siamese desserts—Thong Yip and Thong Yot—confectionary inventions by one of my courtiers."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DELEGATION_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我送来了暹罗点心——蛋黄花和蛋黄球——我的甜品师精心准备的糖果。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Your delegation is welcome. I will have my royal playwrights prepare a Khon drama to recieve them."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "欢迎你的代表团。我会让我的剧作家准备一出暹罗舞剧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Siam politely refuses your delegation. We have no need for your gifts, but thank you nonetheless."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "暹罗礼貌地拒绝你的代表团。我们不需要你的礼物，但是我们依然十分感谢。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Your words are unbecoming of a righteous and virtuous ruler, and I will not let them touch me."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "你的言辞不符合以为正直统治者的形象，我不会让它影响到我。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "I try to be understanding of foreign ways, but I cannot let your unrighteous behavior pass without reproach."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我尝试理解你的做法，但强烈谴责你的倒行逆施。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "We are good friends, are we not? Would you be amenable to deepening this relationship with an alliance?"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我们是好朋友，是吗？你是否愿意将这段关系深化为盟约呢？"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_GREETING_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Good day."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_GREETING_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "你好。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Impossible."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "不可能。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Excellent, I'll have the Phrakhlang manage the details."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "很好，我会让财政部处理这笔交易。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Let us open our mutual borders in the spirit of friendship and commerce!"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "为了友谊和商业，让我们互相开放边界吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "I grant you free passage through the lands of Siam."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我准许你进入暹罗的领土。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Until I can be sure of your intentions, I cannot grant you this."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "在我了解你的真实意图之前，我不会授予你通行权。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Do not presume you can keep your soldiers on my borders without repercussions. Move them at once."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "不要以为我注意不到你在边界陈兵。立刻将他们移走。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "May our embassies go and come without interruption, and may our friendship be strong and everlasting."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "让我们的使馆畅行无阻，我们的友谊地久天长。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_RENEW_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "My august friend; I pray you will wish to continue our alliance? We have both profited greatly from it."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_RENEW_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我的挚友，我希望你愿意继续我们的盟约。我们都从中收获良多。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_RENEW_ALLIANCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Yes! I shall send you gifts in celebration of our continued alliance."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_RENEW_ALLIANCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "很好。我将送你礼品以纪念我们友谊的延续。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_RENEW_ALLIANCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "We regret to say, that Siam is unwilling to continue the alliance at this time. Our sincere apologies."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_RENEW_ALLIANCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我很遗憾地通知你，暹罗这次将不会续签盟约。我们诚挚地道歉。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_RENEW_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "Wonderful! Thank you, my merchants will be greatly pleased to hear the news. As am I, of course."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_RENEW_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "非常感谢。我们的商人很愿意听到这样的消息。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_RENEW_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "I cannot force you to agree, but I think you come to realise the mistake you've made."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_RENEW_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_ANY", "我不会强迫你同意，但是你将会知道这是一个错误。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_NARAI_QUOTE", "May our embassies go and come without interruption, and may our friendship be strong and everlasting."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_NARAI_QUOTE", "愿我们的大使馆不受干扰地来往，愿我们的友谊强大而持久。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_NARAI_TITLE", "Narai"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_NARAI_TITLE", "那莱"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_NARAI_SUBTITLE", "Somdet Phra Narai Maharat"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_SUK_NARAI_SUBTITLE", "那莱大帝"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_CAPSULE_BODY", "As in history, Siam is a center of diplomacy and commerce. Narai doubles down on the diplomacy, providing potent bonuses to maintaining alliances."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_CAPSULE_BODY", "在历史上，暹罗是一个外交和商业的中心。那莱在外交方面加倍努力，为维持联盟提供有力的奖励。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_DETAILED_BODY", "Siam is an unrivaled diplomat, gaining an additional Envoy when completing any Civic that already provides them. The City-State friends they gain will provide useful yield boosts to Siam’s districts. To help aid with this, place districts next to a river to gain extra [ICON_Amenities] Amenities to aid with expansion. Siam’s Floating Markets will incentivise grabbing Luxury Resources as well, providing [ICON_Culture] Culture and [ICON_Gold] Gold when working them, so keep that in mind when founding your cities. Narai extends Siam’s diplomatic prowess to other major players as well, with additional benefits for maintaining alliances, and for trading."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_DETAILED_BODY", "暹罗是一个无与伦比的外交家，当完成任何已经提供使者的市政时，会获得一个额外的使者。他们获得的城邦朋友将为暹罗的地区提供有用的收益提升。为了帮助实现这一目标，将地区放在河流旁边可以获得额外的 [ICON_Amenities] 宜居度以帮助扩张。暹罗的水上市场也会激励人们去抢夺奢侈资源，在使用它们时提供 [ICON_Culture] 文化和 [ICON_Gold] 金币，所以在建立城市时要记住这一点。那莱将暹罗的外交能力扩展到其他主要文明，为维持联盟和贸易提供额外的好处。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "King Narai the Great or Ramathibodi III was the 27th monarch of Ayutthaya Kingdom, the 4th and the last monarch of the Prasat Thong dynasty. He was the king of Ayutthaya Kingdom from 1656 to 1688 and arguably the most famous king of the Prasat Thong dynasty."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "那莱大帝或拉玛铁菩提三世是阿瑜陀耶王国的第27位君主，也是巴沙通王朝王朝的第四位和最后一位君主。他是1656年至1688年阿瑜陀耶王国的国王，可以说是巴沙通王朝最著名的国王。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "Narai was a son of King Prasat Thong by a queen who was a daughter of King Song Tham, and he came to the throne after violent palace upheavals had cut short the reigns of his elder brother and his uncle. He was an effective ruler who dealt successfully with Siam’s traditional Southeast Asian rivals and was ambitious to thrust his kingdom onto the stage of world politics. Domestic policies in King Narai's reign were greatly affected by the interference of foreign powers most notably the Chinese to the north, the Dutch to the South, and the English who were making their first forays into India to the west. Policies revolved around either directly countering the influence, or creating a delicate balance of power between the different parties."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "那莱是巴沙通国王的儿子，他的王后是宋谭王的女儿，他是在宫廷剧烈动荡缩短了他哥哥和他叔叔的统治之后登上王位的。他是一个有效的统治者，成功地处理了暹罗在东南亚的传统对手，并雄心勃勃地将他的王国推上世界政治舞台。那莱国王在位期间的国内政策受到外国势力的干扰，特别是北边的中国人、南边的荷兰人和西边首次进入印度的英国人的影响很大。政策围绕着直接对抗影响，或在不同党派之间建立微妙的权力平衡。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "In 1660, the Chinese invaded the Burmese capitol at Ava to capture Zhu Youlang, the last Southern Ming emperor. Sensing a possible weakening of Burmese influence in the northern vassal states, King Narai began the Burmese–Siamese War of 1662–64 to bring Chiang Mai under the direct control of Ayutthya. Although the expedition was successful in taking control of Lampang and other smaller cities, a second expedition had to be conducted to bring Chiang Mai under control in 1662. After stopping a Burmese army incursion in 1663 at Sai Yok, Narai led an army of 60,000 in an invasion of Burma, capturing Martaban, Syriam, Rangoon, Hongsawadi, and then in 1664 laid siege to Pagan. After “causing many casualties in dead and wounded and capturing many prisoners of war”, the Siamese retreated."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "1660年，中国人进攻缅甸首都阿瓦，俘虏了南明最后一位皇帝朱由榔。那莱国王感觉到缅甸在北方诸侯国的影响力可能会减弱，于是开始了1662-64年的缅甸-暹罗战争，将清迈置于阿瑜陀耶王的直接控制之下。虽然这次远征成功地控制了南邦和其他较小的城市，但不得不在1662年进行第二次远征，将清迈置于控制之下。1663年，那莱在赛育阻止了缅甸军队的入侵，之后他率领6万军队入侵缅甸，占领了马达班、沙廉、洪沙瓦底，然后在1664年围攻蒲甘。在“造成大量死伤并俘获许多战俘”后，暹罗人撤退了。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "After ruling from the city of Ayutthaya for ten years, he had the city of Lopburi restored so it could be a reserve capital. King Narai would eventually come to stay in Lopburi for long periods of time, about 8–9 months a year. The official reason for this move was that Lopburi afforded the king plenty of fresh air, and gave him plenty of opportunity for royal hunts, but the move to Lopburi was arguably prompted by the Dutch naval blockade of Ayutthaya in 1664 to enforce a fur monopoly. Lopburi, unlike Ayutthaya, was not vulnerable an attack by sea."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "在阿瑜陀耶府统治了十年之后，他恢复了华富里城，使之成为一个后备首都。那莱国王最终将长期居住在华富里，每年约8-9个月。此举的官方原因是华富里府为国王提供了大量的新鲜空气，并为他提供了大量的皇家狩猎机会，但可以说，搬迁到华富里府是由1664年荷兰海军封锁大城府以实施毛皮垄断所促成的。华富里府与阿瑜陀耶不同，不容易受到海上的攻击。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "The most remarkable aspect of King Narai's reign were the diplomatic missions that he sent and received during his reign. Missions were sent as far afield as France, England, and the Vatican, although at least two missions were lost at sea. Ties with states closer to Ayutthaya were not neglected as missions were also sent to Persia, Golconda (India), China, as well as other neighbouring states. 1662 marked the arrival of more French priests, their quarrels with the Portuguese Jesuits and Dominicans established in Ayutthaya, their vain attempts to heal the paralysis of Chaofa Aphaitot, the king's half-brother, the consecration of Louis Laneau as first Bishop of Ayutthaya, etc. They maintained excellent contacts with the Royal Court. The king was presented with sumptuously bound volumes containing not only copper engravings of biblical scenes, but also of Louis XIV, the royal palaces, vistas of Paris, and so on."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "那莱国王在位期间最引人注目的是他所派遣和接待的外交使团。派出的使团远至法国、英国和梵蒂冈，尽管至少有两个使团在海上失踪。与阿瑜陀耶近在咫尺的国家的关系也没有被忽视，因为还向波斯、戈尔康达（印度）、中国以及其他邻国派出了使团。1662年，更多的法国神父来到大城，他们与在大城建立的葡萄牙耶稣会士和多明我会士发生争执，他们试图医治国王同父异母的兄弟昭发·阿百多的瘫痪，并祝贺路易·兰奈成为阿瑜陀耶的第一位主教，等等。他们与皇家宫廷保持着良好的联系。他们向国王赠送了装订豪华的画册，其中不仅有圣经场景的铜版画，还有路易十四、王宫、巴黎的远景等等。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "Narai was very curious about the world outside Siam and he listened eagerly to these eulogies. The idea seeped (or was seeped) in to his mind that diplomatic contacts with so powerful a prince would enhance his status among the rulers of Southeast Asia and. rein in the Dutch. Their arrogance and power in the region worried him, and he never truly forgave nor forgot the 1663 blockade of the Chao Phraya river mouth. The French bishops Lambert and Laneau urged him to send an embassy to Versailles, and the agents of the Royal Company offered him passage for his envoys on the Soleil d'Orient. The King dispatched a lavish and vast embassy. Court astrologers had predicted all kinds of disasters for Siamese reckless enough to board western vessels, and events proved them to be right. The Soleil d'Orient left Bantam in August 1681, but never reached her destination. The hapless vessel likely perished somewhere between Madagascar and the Cape, with Siamese and French official suspecting Dutch interference."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "那莱对暹罗以外的世界非常好奇，他热切地聆听着这些赞美之词。他认为与如此强大的王子进行外交接触会提高他在东南亚统治者中的地位，并能遏制荷兰人。他们在该地区的傲慢和权力令他担忧，他从未真正原谅或忘记1663年对湄南河口的封锁。法国主教兰伯（Lambert）和兰奈（Laneau）敦促他向凡尔赛派遣一个使团，皇家公司的代理人为他的使节提供了东方之光号的通行证。国王派出了一个奢华而庞大的使团。宫廷占卜师曾预言暹罗人鲁莽地登上西方船只会有各种灾难，事实证明他们是对的。东方之光号于1681年8月离开万丹，但从未到达目的地。这艘不幸的船很可能在马达加斯加和开普之间的某个地方沉没，暹罗人和法国官员怀疑是荷兰人的干涉。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "It would not be until later that Narai would try again. In the interval a Greek adventurer with the Latinized name of Constantine Phaulkon who formerly worked for the English East India Company was introduced into the court in 1681 as a skilled interpreter and quickly gained royal favor. He became a favourite of Narai, and urged the king to pursue his overtures towards the French. A modest mission of two nobles and a French priest to act as interpreter, set off for France in January 1684 on a small British vessel and reached Paris safely before the end of the year. They were recieved personally by Louis XIV in the Gallery of Mirrors in Versailles. The king said to him in his usual royal manner: “Please assure these gentlemen that I am delighted to have seen them, and that I shall comply with the utmost pleasure with the wishes of my brother the king of Siam”. In response, Louis XIV appointed Alexandre de Chaumont as his ambassador, and assigned the Abbe de Choisy as counsel and possible replacement. Six Jesuits, well-grounded in astronomy and mathematics, were to sail with the ambassador on the Oiseau and Maligne."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "直到后来，那莱才再次尝试。在这期间，一位曾为英国东印度公司工作的希腊冒险家君士坦丁·华尔康（Constantine Phaulkon）于1681年作为一名熟练的翻译被引入宫廷，并迅速获得了皇家的青睐。他成为纳莱的宠臣，并敦促国王继续向法国人示好。1684年1月，由两名贵族和一名充当翻译的法国牧师组成的小型代表团乘坐一艘小型英国船只前往法国，并在年底前安全抵达巴黎。他们在凡尔赛的镜廊受到了路易十四的亲自接见。国王以他一贯的皇家方式对他说“请向这些先生们保证，我很高兴看到他们，而且我将非常高兴地满足我弟弟暹罗国王的愿望。”作为回应，路易十四任命亚历山大·德·修蒙（Alexandre de Chaumont）为他的大使，并指派乔西神父（Abbe de Choisy）担任顾问和可能的替代者。六名精通天文学和数学的耶稣会士将与大使一起乘坐飞鸟号和玛琳号航行。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_8", "The two vessels returned to France with an important Siamese embassy, a letter on gold foil and magnificent presents for the King and the Royal Family. The three ambassadors were selected with great care. The first ambassador was no one less than Okphra Visut Sunthorn, better known as Kosa Pan, who had shared a wet nurse with Phra Narai and was raised with him. The second and third ambassadors were outstanding mandarins with diplomatic experience. In June 1686 the two vessels dropped anchor in the seaport of Brest in Brittany after a smooth return voyage of hardly six months. All along the journey the three Siamese ambassadors had prepared themselves eagerly for their mission in France, asking lost of questions and taking notes. Father Vachet, who escorted them, was very helpful in this respect. We are very well informed about the eight months the Siamese delegation spent in France. Father Vachet's Memoirs, and the Diaries kept by several French courtiers such as Sourches and Dangeau, provide us with a wealth of details. But the most impressive source is the monthly Mercure galant which devoted no less than 2,000 small pages to the Siamese embassy."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_8", "这两艘船带着重要的暹罗使团、金箔信和给国王和王室的华丽礼物返回法国。这三位大使是经过精心挑选的。第一位大使是威拉·桑索恩，也就是众所周知的戈沙班，他曾与那莱王共用一个奶妈，并与他一起长大。第二和第三位大使是具有外交经验的杰出官员。1686年6月，这两艘船在经历了近6个月的顺利回航后，在布列塔尼的布雷斯特海港抛锚。一路上，三位暹罗大使都在为他们在法国的使命做着热切的准备，问了很多问题并做了很多笔记。护送他们的瓦歇神父在这方面帮助很大。我们对暹罗代表团在法国度过的八个月有很完善的了解。瓦歇神父的《回忆录》以及苏克西和丹戈等几位法国朝臣的日记为我们提供了大量的细节。但是，最令人印象深刻的资料是《风雅信使》月刊，它用了不少于2000个小页的篇幅来介绍暹罗国大使。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_9", "But this is where things begin to fall apart. Phaulkon was desperate for a French presence in Siam on which he could rely in case of emergency. He offered the fortresses of Bangkok and Mergui, the two “keys of the kingdom,” to the French. Thus the return mission carried soldiers to garrison these fortresses. Father Tachard managed to disembark well ahead of the others and to meet Phaulkon before Kosa Pan and his colleagues could advise against the cession of Bangkok and Mergui. The Greek convinced Phra Narai and his Council to put the two strongholds under French “protection.” Phra Phetracha, chief of the elephantry, was the only member of the Council to speak against the proposal, which was in the end approved by the king. Phetracha became in no time the heart of a nationalist anti-French movement, which was joined soon after by Kromluang Yothathep, Phra Narai's strongheaded daughter."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_9", "但这正是事情开始崩溃的地方。华尔康迫切希望法国人在暹罗的存在，在紧急情况下他可以依赖法国人。他把曼谷和丹老这两个“王国的钥匙”的要塞提供给法国人。因此，回国的代表团携带士兵驻守这些要塞。塔夏尔神父设法在其他人之前上岸，并在戈沙班和他的同事提出反对割让曼谷和丹老的建议之前见到了华尔康。希腊人说服了那莱和他的理事会，将这两个据点置于法国人的“保护”之下。象队统领帕碧罗阇（Phra Phetracha）是议会中唯一反对该提案的成员，该提案最终得到了国王的批准。帕碧罗阇很快就成为反法民族主义运动的核心，不久之后，那莱的强势女儿约萨西普也加入了这个运动。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_10", "Matters were brought to a head when King Narai fell gravely ill in March 1688 while the king stayed in Lopburi palaces. Aware of the coming succession dispute, in May 1688 Narai called together his closest councillors: Phaulkon, Phra Phetracha, and Mom Pi and nominated his daughter, Kromluang Yothathep to succeed him. The three councillors were to act as regents until the princess took on a partner of her choice from one of the two Siamese councillors. But when Narai was seriously ill with no hope of recovery, Phetracha arrested Phaulkon and the French officers. After questioning Mom Pi, he discovered Mom Pi had conspired with Phaulkon to assume the throne, and Mom Pi was executed. Further questioning of Phaulkon revealed a plot to raise a rebellion, and he too was executed. Narai, on his deathbed, was unable to do anything, except curse Phetracha and his son, Luang Sorasak. Luang Sorasak then had Narai's two brothers executed. On the death of King Narai, Phetracha proclaimed himself king. Siamese troops attacked the French troops during the Siege of Bangkok. Finally, the French soldiers were allowed to return to France. Thus ended the era of French influence in Siam."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_10", "1688年3月，那莱国王在华富里宫得了重病，事情陷入了困境。意识到即将到来的继承权争端，1688年5月，纳莱召集了他最亲密的顾问。华尔康、帕碧罗阇和亚派耶脱，并提名他的女儿约萨西普继任。这三位议员将作为摄政者，直到公主从两位暹罗议员中选择一个伴侣。但是，当那莱病重，没有康复的希望时，帕碧罗阇逮捕了华尔康和法国官员。在审问了亚派耶脱之后，他发现亚派耶脱与华尔康密谋夺取王位，亚派耶脱被处决。对华尔康的进一步审问发现他有发动叛乱的阴谋，他也被处决。那莱在临终前什么也做不了，只能诅咒帕碧罗阇和他的儿子琅索拉萨。琅索拉萨随后将那莱的两个兄弟处决。那莱国王死后，菲特拉查宣布自己为国王。暹罗军队在围攻曼谷期间袭击了法国军队。最后，法国士兵被允许返回法国。至此，法国在暹罗的影响时代结束。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_11", "Although King Narai's reign witnessed the greatest extent of foreign influence at the Siamese court, his diplomatic achievements were to be reversed by his successor. It is debatable whether the new introspective attitude of his successors contributed to the weakening and eventual fall of Ayutthaya. Nevertheless, his reign's diplomatic achievements contributed to him being posthumously styled “the Great,” one of seven recognised as such in the history of Thailand. At the same time, the records of those involved in the diplomatic missions, particularly those from the west, have allowed historians to obtain a rare glimpse into the world of the Ayutthayan court as most original Ayutthaya records were destroyed with the city in 1767. These include the French accounts of the Chevalier de Chaumont, the Abbé de Choisy, Fr. Tachard, Claude de Forbin, de la Loubere and the Persian account of Muhammad Rabi' ibn Muhammad Ibrahim. Domestically, the relative stability during his reign also gave rise to the revival of Siamese literature during his reign. In addition, among the gifts that were exchanged between the Siamese and the French courts, two items from Siam were to have an unexpected impact on French history. The items were a pair of silver cannons that were eventually stored in the Royal Furniture Repository in Paris since they were classed as gifts rather than weapons. On the 14th of July, 1789, rioting Parisians discovered these cannons and hauled them over to the Bastille."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_SUK_NARAI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_11", "尽管那莱国王在位期间见证了暹罗宫廷中最大程度的外国影响，但他的外交成就却被他的继任者推翻了。他的继任者的新的内省态度是否促成了阿瑜陀耶的衰弱和最终衰落，这一点值得商榷。然而，他在位期间的外交成就使他被追认为“大帝”，是泰国历史上公认的七个大帝之一。同时，参与外交使团的记录，特别是来自西方的记录，使历史学家能够罕见地窥见大城王朝的宫廷世界，因为大多数大城王朝的原始记录都在1767年随着城市被摧毁。这些记录包括法国德·修蒙、乔西神父、塔夏尔神父、克洛德·德·福尔班、德·拉·鲁布的记录以及波斯穆罕默德·拉比·伊本·穆罕默德·易卜拉欣的记录。在国内，他统治时期的相对稳定也催生了暹罗文学在他统治时期的复兴。此外，在暹罗和法国宫廷之间交换的礼物中，有两件来自暹罗的物品对法国历史产生了意外的影响。这两件物品是一对银质大炮，由于被列为礼物而非武器，最终被存放在巴黎的皇家家具库。1789年7月14日，起义的巴黎人发现了这些大炮，并把它们拖到了巴士底狱。");

