("en_US", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SWAHILI_SIZE", "Est. 426 thousand square miles (1,104.3 thousand square km)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SWAHILI_SIZE", "约42.6万平方英里（110.43万平方公里）。"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SWAHILI_POPULATION", "99.4 million (2015 est.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SWAHILI_POPULATION", "约9940万人（2015年数据）"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SWAHILI_CAPITAL", "Not a unified state with a capital, but major cities include  Kilwa, Malindi, Mombasa, Pate, Sofala and Zanzibar."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVINFO_SUK_SWAHILI_CAPITAL", "并非有一个首都的统一国家。主要城市有基尔瓦，马林迪，蒙巴萨，帕特，索法拉和桑给巴尔"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "The medieval sites along the Swahili Coast represent a single cultural tradition with diverse local traditions that can be traced to the ninth century, which is considered to have developed into the modern Swahili culture. Currently, there are 173 identified settlements that flourished along the Swahili Coast and nearby Islands from the ninth to the seventeenth centuries, which include the sites of Kilwa, Malindi, Gedi, Pate, Comoros and Zanzibar."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "斯瓦西里海岸上的中世纪遗址反应了一种具有不同地方特色的统一文化传统。它们可以追溯到公元九世纪，并且被认为发展成了现在的斯瓦西里文化。现在斯瓦西里海岸上和周边岛屿已经发现了173个建立于九至十七世纪的斯瓦西里据点，包括基尔瓦，马林迪，杰迪，帕特，科摩罗和桑给巴尔。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "Wa-swahili, or “shore people”, designates the inhabitants of the East African coastline, and signifies above all a culture with a common language, Kiswahili, and the same religion, Islam. Arab-Persian geographers referred to the inhabitants of the East African coast as the Zanj. It was at the beginning of the nineteenth century that the first use of the term “Swahili” appeared, with settlers trying to classify and differentiate the different populations of Africa. The Swahilis have defined themselves as such since the colonial period, but differentiate between themselves according to their region, island or town of origin. Despite some common ground, Swahili identity remains multiple, incorporating populations of diverse background, both Cushitic and Bantu."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "瓦-斯瓦西里，又名“海岸上的人”，指的是东非海岸线上居民，大体上拥有共同的文化、语言（斯瓦西里语）和宗教（伊斯兰教）。阿拉伯-波斯的地理学家将东非海岸的居民称为僧祇人。直到十一世纪，“斯瓦西里”这个称呼才出现，用来区分非洲不同地域的民族。在殖民时期，斯瓦西里人才产生认同，但是根据地域、岛屿和祖籍不同有区别。尽管有一些共同点，斯瓦希里人的民族仍然是多样的，包含了不同民族背景的人口，包括库希特人和班图人。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "At the beginning of the first millenium CE, the discovery of the monsoon winds and the means to use them created a nautical revolution, allowing for major water crossings toward India and Ceylon. From the ninth century onward, Muslim geographers mention regular trade relations with East Africa, Zanzibar, Pemba and Sofala. These sources indicate that as early as the ninth century, there were major shipping routes between Asia and Africa."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "在公元一千年之初，季风的发现和利用季风的手段创造了一场航海革命，使人们可以在水面上向印度和锡兰岛进行重大跨越。从第九世纪开始，穆斯林地理学家提到与东非、桑给巴尔、奔巴和索法拉的定期贸易关系。这些资料表明，早在九世纪，亚洲和非洲之间就有了主要的航运路线。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "As a result of this burgeoning trade, the transition between the eleventh and twelfth century was a period of change. A number of urban East African centers developed at this time as did architecture in stone, used for public buildings, mosques and enclosure walls. The Swahili city-states were established. By the thirteenth century, a new balance of power had developed. The Swahili coast was divided into several independent sultanates, including Kilwa, Mombasa, Malindi, Pate and Mogadishu."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "由于这种贸易的蓬勃发展，11世纪和12世纪之间的过渡期中产生了许多变化。一些东非的城市在这个时期发展起来，石制建筑也随之发展，它们用于公共建筑、清真寺和围墙，斯瓦希里城邦由是建立。到13世纪，新的权力平衡已经形成。斯瓦希里海岸分为几个独立的苏丹国，包括基尔瓦、蒙巴萨、马林迪、佩泰和摩加迪沙。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "Kilwa was supposedly one of the most beautiful towns in the world with stone houses covered with palm-leaf roofs or makuti; only certain mosques and the palace had hard flat roofs. From the fourteenth to fifteenth century, Kilwa continued to hold the monopoly for gold, trading gold from Yufi, situated a one-month walk from the coast. Sofala, a vassal of Kilwa city, maintained commercial relations with the Shona kingdom of Great Zimbabwe; the rise of Great Zimbabwe was intimately linked to the trading of gold with Islamized peoples."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "据说，基尔瓦是世界上建设得最为美丽的城市之一，房顶由棕榈叶铺成。只有清真寺和王宫有硬质屋顶。从十四到十五世纪，基尔瓦垄断了的黄金贸易。基尔瓦的附庸索法拉与大津巴布韦的修纳王国保持着商业关系；大津巴布韦的崛起与伊斯兰民族的黄金贸易有着密切的联系。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "The arrival of the Portuguese explorer Vasco da Gama in 1498 signaled a new era of foreign rule on the Swahili Coast. On a mission to economically control and Christianize the Swahili coast, the Portuguese attacked Kilwa first in 1505 and other cities later. Because of Swahili resistance, the Portuguese attempt at establishing commercial control was never successful. By the late 17th century, Portuguese authority on the Swahili coast began to diminish. With the help of Omani Arabs, by 1729 the Portuguese presence had been removed. The Swahili coast eventually became part of the Sultanate of Oman. Trade recovered, but it did not regain the levels of the past."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "1498年，葡萄牙探险家瓦斯科·达·伽马的到来，标志着斯瓦希里海岸进入了一个新的外国统治时代。在对斯瓦希里海岸进行经济控制和基督教化的任务中，葡萄牙人于1505年首先袭击了基尔瓦，后来又袭击了其他城市。由于斯瓦希里人的抵抗，葡萄牙人建立经济控制的尝试从未完全成功。到17世纪末，葡萄牙人在斯瓦希里海岸的统治力度开始减弱。在阿曼阿拉伯人的帮助下，到1729年，葡萄牙人的存在已经被清除。斯瓦希里海岸最终成为阿曼苏丹国的一部分。贸易有所恢复，但并没有恢复到过去的水平。 "),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "The Swahili civilization stands at the periphery of the Muslim and African worlds, resulting in the development of a unique coastal culture based on trade. In fact, its marginal position is linked to our vision of the Indian Ocean, which separates Africa, Arabia and Asia. But the ocean also provides a connection between these very different cultures: the Swahilis are thus dynamic players, equal to Arab, Persian and Indian traders. Swahili archaeology is at the crossroads of Islamic archaeology and African archaeology."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "斯瓦希里文明站在穆斯林和非洲世界的边缘，导致了基于贸易的独特沿海文化的发展。事实上，它的边缘地位与我们对印度洋的看法有关，它将非洲、阿拉伯和亚洲分开。但是，海洋也为这些非常不同的文化提供了联系：因此，斯瓦希里人是充满活力的参与者，与阿拉伯、波斯和印度的商人平等。斯瓦希里考古学处于伊斯兰考古学和非洲考古学的十字路口。"),
("en_US", "LOC_CIVILIZATION_SUK_SWAHILI_NAME", "Swahili"),
