("en_US", "LOC_UNIT_SUK_JAHAZI_NAME", "Jahazi"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_UNIT_SUK_JAHAZI_NAME", "贾哈兹方舟"),
("en_US", "LOC_UNIT_SUK_JAHAZI_DESCRIPTION", "Swahili unique Ancient era support unit. Embarked units within 2 tiles ignore terrain costs and receive +1 [ICON_Movement] Movement. Has 2 charges to build Fishing Boats. Fishing Boats built by a Jahazi yield +1 [ICON_Production] Production, +2 [ICON_Gold] Gold. Unlocks with Sailing."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_UNIT_SUK_JAHAZI_DESCRIPTION", "斯瓦希里特色远古时代支援单位。为两个单元格内的水运单位提供+1 [ICON_Movement] 移动力，并无视海洋地貌带来的 [ICON_Movement] 移动力惩罚。获得+2使用次数，能够建造渔船，建造的渔船获得+1 [ICON_Production] 生产力和+2 [ICON_Gold] 金币。"), --为相邻的水域提供+1 [ICON_Food] 粮食和+1 [ICON_Production] 生产力。如果在友方领土内，为两个单元格内您的海军单位每回合+20生命值。
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_UNITS_PAGE_UNIT_SUK_JAHAZI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "The largest traditional sailing vessel in wide use off the coast of East Africa is the jahazi, which measures up to 20m long and whose large billowing sails are a characteristic sight off Zanzibar and other traditional ports. With a capacity of about a hundred passengers, the jahazi is mainly used for transporting cargo and passengers over relatively long distances or in open water, for instance between Dar es Salaam and Zanzibar. Minor modifications in the Portuguese and Omani eras notwithstanding, the design of the modern jahazi is pretty much identical to that of similar seafaring vessels used in medieval times and before. The name jahazi is generally applied to boats with cutaway bows and square sterns built on Zanzibar and nearby parts of the mainland."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_UNITS_PAGE_UNIT_SUK_JAHAZI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "在东非沿海广泛使用的最大的传统帆船是贾哈兹方舟，它长达20米，其巨大的船帆是桑给巴尔和其他传统港口的特色景观。贾哈兹方舟的载客量约为100人，主要用于在相对较长的距离或在开放水域运输货物和乘客，例如在达累斯萨拉姆和桑给巴尔之间。尽管在葡萄牙和阿曼时代有一些小的修改，但现代贾哈兹方舟的设计与中世纪及以前使用的类似航海船只基本相同。贾哈兹这个名字一般适用于在桑给巴尔岛和大陆附近地区建造的船，船头是镂空的，船尾是方形的。"),
("en_US", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_YIELD_BOOST_NAME", "Juya Nets"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_YIELD_BOOST_NAME", "围网捕捞"),
("en_US", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_YIELD_BOOST_DESCRIPTION", "+1 [ICON_Food] Food and +1 [ICON_Production] Production to adjacent water tiles"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_YIELD_BOOST_DESCRIPTION", "为相邻的水域提供+1 [ICON_Food] 粮食和+1 [ICON_Production] 生产力"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_DESCRIPTION", "为两个单元格内的水运单位提供+1 [ICON_Movement] 移动力，并无视海洋地貌带来的 [ICON_Movement] 移动力惩罚。[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET] 能够建造渔船，建造的渔船获得+1 [ICON_Production] 生产力和+2 [ICON_Gold] 金币。"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_EMBARKED_MOVEMENT_DESCRIPTION", "为两个单元格内的水运单位提供+1 [ICON_Movement] 移动力，并无视海洋地貌带来的 [ICON_Movement] 移动力惩罚。"),
("en_US", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_YIELD_BOOST_DESCRIPTION_XP2", "If on a water tile adjacent to a Jahazi, Features provide +2 [ICON_Culture] Culture, and Fishing Boats provide +2 [ICON_Gold] Gold. Features on water tiles adjacent to a Jahazi provide +2 [ICON_Tourism] Tourism after researching Conservation"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_YIELD_BOOST_DESCRIPTION_XP2", "为相邻的海洋地貌提供+2 [ICON_Culture] 文化，渔船+2 [ICON_Gold] 金币。相邻的海洋地貌在研究“保护地球”后+2 [ICON_Tourism] 旅游业绩如果在友方领土内"),
("en_US", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_ADJACENT_HEAL_NAME", "Kamal"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_ADJACENT_HEAL_NAME", "舰队补给"),
("en_US", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_ADJACENT_HEAL_DESCRIPTION", "While this unit is in friendly territory, your Naval units within 2 tiles heal +20 HP per turn"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_ABILITY_SUK_JAHAZI_ADJACENT_HEAL_DESCRIPTION", "为两个单元格内您的海军单位每回合+20生命值"),
("en_US", "LOC_BUILDING_SUK_PILLAR_TOMB_NAME", "Pillar Tomb"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_BUILDING_SUK_PILLAR_TOMB_NAME", "柱陵"),
("en_US", "LOC_BUILDING_SUK_PILLAR_TOMB_DESCRIPTION", "A building unique to the Swahili. It is cheaper than the Monument which it replaces. +1 [ICON_Culture] Culture, Provides +1 Loyalty per turn in this city. If the city already has maximum Loyalty, also provides an additional +1 [ICON_Culture] Culture. After Calendar is researched, provides an additional +1 [ICON_CULTURE] Culture. International [ICON_TradeRoute] Trade Routes from this city generate +1 [ICON_Gold] Gold, +1 [ICON_Culture] Culture for each of this city’s districts that are within 2 tiles of the City Centre."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_BUILDING_SUK_PILLAR_TOMB_DESCRIPTION", "取代纪念碑的斯瓦希里特色建筑。比纪念碑更便宜。提供+1 [ICON_Culture] 文化值。使此城每回合+1忠诚度。若城市忠诚度已达最高，则额外+1 [ICON_Culture] 文化值。研究“历法”科技后，额外+1 [ICON_Culture] 文化值。市中心两个单元格内的每个区域为本城出发的国际 [ICON_TradeRoute] 贸易路线提供+1 [ICON_Culture] 文化值和+1 [ICON_Gold] 金币。"), --每有一位 [ICON_GreatPerson] 伟人在柱陵1格范围内耗尽使用次数或隐退，所在城市则+1 [ICON_Gold] 金币产出(上限为+10 [ICON_Gold] )。
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_BUILDINGS_PAGE_BUILDING_SUK_PILLAR_TOMB_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "One of the most distinctive and enigmatic architectural forms associated with the Swahili were the structures associated with burials. The remains of monumental tomb structures still litter the coastal regions and mark many of the long-vanished centers of Swahili life. The simplest tomb structures were rectangular enclosures, bounded by four low walls, varying in size and scale. The most distinctive and unusual feature of many Swahili medieval tombs was the addition of a tall column-like structure, forming a characteristic building type along the East African coast referred to as pillar tombs. These pillars come in many sizes and shapes, from rounded, square, multisided or fluted and rose to various heights. These pillars, and sometimes parts of the surrounding enclosure walls, were often decorated with inset porcelain or other glazed ceramic bowls imported from southern Arabia, Persia and even as far as China, adding a dash of color to contrast with the brilliant white plaster surfaces, forming a distinctive decorative tradition unique to the medieval East African coast."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_BUILDINGS_PAGE_BUILDING_SUK_PILLAR_TOMB_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "与斯瓦希里人有关的最独特和神秘的建筑形式之一是与墓葬有关的建筑。纪念性坟墓结构的遗迹仍然遍布斯瓦西里沿海地区，标志着许多早已消失的斯瓦希里人的聚落。最简单的墓葬结构是长方形的围墙，由四道低矮的墙围住，大小和规模各不相同。许多斯瓦希里中世纪墓葬最独特和不寻常的特征是增加了一个高大的柱状结构，形成了东非海岸的一种特色建筑类型，被称为柱状墓。这些柱子有很多尺寸和形状，从圆形、方形、多面体或凹槽，并上升到不同的高度。这些柱子，有时是周围围墙的一部分，经常用从阿拉伯南部、波斯甚至远在中国进口的嵌瓷或其他釉面陶瓷碗进行装饰，为辉煌的白色石膏表面增添了一抹色彩，与之形成了中世纪东非海岸特有的装饰传统。"),
("en_US", "LOC_LEADER_SUK_AL_HASAN_NAME", "Al-Hasan ibn Sulaiman"),
