("en_US", "LOC_CIVINFO_CVS_ARMENIA_CAPITAL", "Yerevan"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_CIVINFO_CVS_ARMENIA_CAPITAL", "埃里温"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ARMENIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "The ancient Kingdom of Armenia was an independent monarchy from 331 BC to AD 428. When the kingdom was the most powerful it was also called the Armenian Empire. After the fall of the Achaemenid Empire, the former Satrapy of Armenia was divided in about 120 clan territories. After the destruction of the Seleucid Empire, a Helenistic Greek successor state of Alexander the Great's short-lived empire, a Helenistic Armenian state was founded in 190 BC by Artaxias I. At its height, from 95 to 66 BC, Armenia extended its rule through areas of the Caucasus and the area that is now eastern Turkey, Syria and Lebanon. Armenia was one of the weakest states in the Roman East. It was under the Roman sphere of influence in 66 BC."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ARMENIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "古代亚美尼亚王国是一个独立的君主国，从公元前331年到公元428年。当这个王国最强大的时候，它也被称为亚美尼亚帝国。阿契美尼德帝国灭亡后，前亚美尼亚总督辖地被划分为大约120个氏族领地。塞琉古帝国是亚历山大大帝短命帝国的希腊化继承国，在塞琉古帝国被摧毁后，公元前190年，阿尔塔西亚斯一世建立了一个希腊化的亚美尼亚国家。在其鼎盛时期，即公元前95年至66年，亚美尼亚将其统治延伸到高加索地区以及现在的土耳其东部、叙利亚和黎巴嫩地区。此时亚美尼亚是罗马东方最弱的国家之一。公元前66年，它处于罗马的势力范围内。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ARMENIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "Armenia reached its greatest size and influence under King Tigranes II. It went from the Mediterranean Sea northeast to the Kura River. The Artaxiads were overthrown by the Romans in AD 12. This started a period of civil war. After AD 54, the kingdom was ruled by the Arsacid Dynasty. In AD 387, Armenia was divided into Byzantine Armenia in the west and Persian Armenia in the east. Persian Armenia remained under the rule of Arsacid client kings until AD 428."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ARMENIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "亚美尼亚在提格兰二世国王时期达到了最大的规模和影响力。它从地中海向东北延伸至库拉河。公元12年，阿尔塔西亚斯王朝被罗马人推翻了。亚美尼亚开始了一个内战时期。公元54年后，该王国由阿萨希德王朝统治。公元387年，亚美尼亚被划分为西部的拜占庭亚美尼亚和东部的波阿萨希德王朝的藩王统治。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ARMENIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "The Arsacid Dynasty ruled the Kingdom of Armenia from 54 to 428. They used to be a branch of the Parthian Arsacids but became a distinctly Armenian dynasty later on. Arsacid Kings reigned intermittently throughout the chaotic years after the fall of the Artaxiad Dynasty until 62 when Tiridates I of Armenia secured Arsacid rule in Armenia. An independent line of Kings was established by Vologases II of Armenia in 180. Two of the most notable events under Arsacid rule in Armenian history were the conversion of Armenia to Christianity by St. Gregory the Illuminator in 301 and the creation of the Armenian alphabet by Mesrop Mashtots in 405."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_CIVILIZATIONS_PAGE_CIVILIZATION_CVS_ARMENIA_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "阿萨希德王朝从54年到428年统治着亚美尼亚王国。他们曾经是帕提亚阿萨希德王朝的一个分支，但后来成为一个亚美尼亚王朝。阿尔塔西亚斯灭亡后，在整个混乱的年代里，阿萨希德家族国王断断续续地进行统治，直到62年，亚美尼亚的提里达特一世确保了阿萨希德王朝在亚美尼亚的统治。180年，亚美尼亚的沃洛伽斯二世建立了一个独立的王系。在亚美尼亚历史上，阿萨希德王朝统治下最值得注意的两件事是：301年启明者圣格雷戈里使亚美尼亚皈依基督教，以及405年圣梅斯罗布创造亚美尼亚字母。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_DISTRICTS_PAGE_DISTRICT_CVS_ARMENIA_UI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "The earliest Christian accounts of the introduction of Christianity into Armenia date from the 1st century. The Church teaches that it was first preached by two Apostles of Jesus, St. Thaddeus and St. Bartholomew. The Armenian Apostolic Church claims to been in existence since the days of the apostles and therefore would be one of the oldest denominations of Christianity. Armenia was the first country to adopt Christianity as its official religion, when St. Gregory the Illuminator converted Tiridates III (the King of Armenia) and members of his court, traditionally dated to 301. The Church teaches that St. Gregory was imprisoned by Tiridates in an underground pit, called Khor Virab, for 13 years, after which he healed the King of an incurable disease, whereupon Tiridates accepted Christianity."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_DISTRICTS_PAGE_DISTRICT_CVS_ARMENIA_UI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "关于基督教传入亚美尼亚的最早记载可以追溯到1世纪。教会认为，它最早是由耶稣的两个使徒，即圣达陡和圣巴多罗买所宣扬。亚美尼亚使徒教会声称自使徒时代就已存在，因此将是基督教最古老的教派之一。亚美尼亚是第一个采用基督教作为其官方宗教的国家，当时启明者圣格雷戈里使提里达特三世（亚美尼亚国王）和他的宫廷成员皈依，传统记载的时间是301年。教会认为，圣格雷戈里被提里达特囚禁在一个名为霍瑞维拉的地下坑道中13年，之后他治愈了国王的不治之症，提里达特也因此接受了基督教。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_DISTRICTS_PAGE_DISTRICT_CVS_ARMENIA_UI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "Armenian architecture, as it originates in an earthquake-prone region, tends to be built with this hazard in mind. Armenian buildings tend to be rather low-slung and thick-walled in design. Armenia has abundant resources of stone, and relatively few forests, so stone was nearly always used throughout for large buildings. Small buildings and most residential buildings were normally constructed of lighter materials, and hardly any early examples survive, as at the abandoned medieval capital of Ani."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_DISTRICTS_PAGE_DISTRICT_CVS_ARMENIA_UI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "亚美尼亚的建筑，由于它起源于地震多发地区，在建造时往往会考虑到这种危险。亚美尼亚的建筑往往是低矮的、厚壁的设计。亚美尼亚拥有丰富的石材资源，而森林相对较少，所以大型建筑几乎都是用石材。小型建筑和大多数住宅建筑通常用较轻的材料建造，几乎没有任何早期的例子存留下来，如被遗弃的中世纪首都阿尼。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_DISTRICTS_PAGE_DISTRICT_CVS_ARMENIA_UI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "The stone used in buildings is typically quarried all at the same location, in order to give the structure a uniform color. In cases where different color stone are used, they are often intentionally contrasted in a striped or checkerboard pattern. Powder made out of ground stone of the same type was often applied along the joints of the tuff slabs to give buildings a seamless look. Unlike the Romans or Syrians who were building at the same time, Armenians never used wood or brick when building large structures."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_DISTRICTS_PAGE_DISTRICT_CVS_ARMENIA_UI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "建筑物中使用的石材通常都是在同一地点开采的，以使结构具有统一的颜色。在使用不同颜色的石头的情况下，它们往往故意形成条纹或格子图案的对比。用同一类型的磨碎的石头制成的粉末常常沿着凝灰岩板的接缝处涂抹，使建筑物看起来天衣无缝。与同时代的罗马人或叙利亚人的建筑不同，亚美尼亚人在建造大型建筑时从不使用木材或砖块。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_DISTRICTS_PAGE_DISTRICT_CVS_ARMENIA_UI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "Armenian architecture employs a form of concrete to produce sturdy buildings. It is a mixture of lime mortar, broken tuff, and rocks around which forms a core against which thin slabs of tuff are arranged in brickwork fashion. As the wet mortar mixture dries it forms a strong concrete-like mass sealed together with the tuff around it and, due to tuff's properties, it becomes harder with time. Initially, almost no core was used in the construction of churches, stone blocks were simply sealed together, but as architects saw how those with mortar cores withstood tremors, the size of the core expanded. Frescos of marble or another stone were often affixed to the side of these buildings, usually at a later date."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_DISTRICTS_PAGE_DISTRICT_CVS_ARMENIA_UI_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "亚美尼亚建筑常用一种特殊形式的混凝土建设。它是一种石灰砂浆、破碎的凝灰岩和岩石的混合物，围绕一个岩石核心排列，凝灰岩的薄板以砖砌的方式排列。随着湿灰泥混合物的干燥，它会形成一只种坚固的混凝土状的块状物，与周围的凝灰岩密封在一起，由于凝灰岩的特性，它随着时间的推移变得更加坚硬。最初，在建造教堂时几乎没有使用核心，石块只是简单地封在一起。但当建筑师发现那些有砂浆核心的教堂可以抵御地震，核心的规模逐渐扩大。大理石或其他石头的壁画经常被贴在这些建筑的侧面，尤其是那些建成时间较晚的建筑。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_UNITS_PAGE_UNIT_CVS_ARMENIA_UU_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "Azatavrear cavalry was the elite guard of Armenian kings. Later, in medieval Azatavrear cavalry was collected from nobles, known as Ayrudzi (man and horse, horseman). During peace time Armenian cavalry was divided into number of small groups which took the role of guarding the King and his family as well as Armenian lords. Other duties of the Armenian cavalry was patrolling Armenian borders under the command of Armenian general (sparapet). The group of Armenian cavalry whose main task was to facilitate the protection of the Armenian king and his family in the ancient period consisted from 6,000 heavy armored horsemen, and in medieval period, 3,000 light armored horsemen. In war time the number of Azatavrear reached from 10,000 up to 20,000 horsemen. Beside Azatavrear cavalry there was Armenian light cavalry, which mainly consisted from horse archers."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_UNITS_PAGE_UNIT_CVS_ARMENIA_UU_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "阿扎塔夫雷尔骑兵是亚美尼亚国王的精锐卫队。后来，在中世纪，阿扎塔夫拉尔骑兵从贵族中征集，被称为艾路兹（人和马，骑手）。在和平时期，亚美尼亚骑兵被分成若干小队，负责保卫国王和他的家人以及亚美尼亚的领主。亚美尼亚骑兵的其他职责是在亚美尼亚将军（sparapet）的指挥下巡逻亚美尼亚边境。在古代时期，亚美尼亚骑兵的主要任务是协助保护亚美尼亚国王和他的家人，包括6000名重装甲骑兵，在中世纪时期，有3000名轻装甲骑兵。在战争时期，阿扎塔夫雷尔的数量从10,000到20,000骑兵。除了阿扎塔夫雷尔骑兵，还有亚美尼亚轻骑兵，主要由马弓手组成。"),
("en_US", "LOC_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_NAME", "Tigranes II"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_NAME", "提格兰二世"),
("en_US", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UA_NAME", "Seventy Valleys"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UA_NAME", "七十谷"),
("en_US", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UA_DESCRIPTION", "Units receive additional [ICON_STRENGTH] Combat Strength on Hills and being [ICON_PROMOTION] Promoted or [ICON_GOLD] Upgraded restores the unit's actions. Cities with an Encampment may build one more district than the [ICON_CITIZEN] Population usually allows."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UA_DESCRIPTION", "无印版效果，不译"),
("en_US", "LOC_AGENDA_CVS_TIGRANES_II_NAME", "Tsovits Tsov"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_AGENDA_CVS_TIGRANES_II_NAME", "从黑海到里海"),
("en_US", "LOC_AGENDA_CVS_TIGRANES_II_DESCRIPTION", "Will not hesitate to backstab others and likes those who endeavour to follow his lead. Thinks civilizations with small militaries are weak."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_AGENDA_CVS_TIGRANES_II_DESCRIPTION", "会毫不犹豫的发动突袭战争并青睐同样做的文明。蔑视军事力量弱小的文明。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_REASON_ANY", "(You have a declared a surprise war.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_REASON_ANY", "（你宣布了一场突袭战争。）"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "Tigranes II is impressed with your brazen approach to surprise wars."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "提格兰二世对你无所顾忌的突袭战争印象深刻。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_REASON_ANY", "(Your military is weak.)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_REASON_ANY", "(你的军队很弱。)"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "Tigranes II thinks you are weak"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MODIFIER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "提格兰二世认为你很弱小。"),
("en_US", "LOC_LOADING_INFO_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II", "Rise, Tigranes the Great. With your fetters removed, now is the time to strike out. Inflict justice upon those unworthy neighbors who profaned your nation, and consolidate their power with yours. Show the world what becomes of those who cross the great stone curtain, and under you, Armenia will know glory."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_LOADING_INFO_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II", "崛起吧，提格兰大帝。已经没有枷锁或障碍可以阻拦你，带领亚美尼亚出击吧。惩罚胆敢侵犯亚美尼亚的邻居，让他们看看进入亚美尼亚石城的下场。在您的领导下，亚美尼亚将走向辉煌。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "I see another ambitious soul hopes to scale the escarpments of Tigranes the Great. Pray ours is a lasting friendship, because to have scaled them, you will have put your back to those escarpments... and my hand on your shoulder."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "啊，我看见这有一个伟大的灵魂来到了我的殿阶前。如果你能信任我并且与我们互相平等相待，我们可以共创未来。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_VISIT_RECIPIENT_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Should you find yourself in the area, I suggest you attend a Kochari dance in our nearest city."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_VISIT_RECIPIENT_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "如果你还愿意留在我们的国家，我建议你在我们最近的城市参加科察里群舞会。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NEAR_INITIATOR_POSITIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Let's strike out then."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NEAR_INITIATOR_POSITIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "让我们开始吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NO_MANS_INFO_EXCHANGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "I extend an invitation to our capital at Tigranocerta, where Hellenistic and Iranian cultures have reached a heretofore unheard of unity--and in hopes of your returning the favor."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_FIRST_MEET_NO_MANS_INFO_EXCHANGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "我向你们发出邀请，请你们到我们在提格拉诺切尔塔的首都来，那里的希腊文化和雅利安文化已经达到了前所未有的统一——希望你们能够同一。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_GREETING_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "Speak freely."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_GREETING_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "畅所欲言吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_GREETING_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "Choose your words wisely."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_GREETING_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "注意你的措辞。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Carry on."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "继续吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "You are not welcome here."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DELEGATION_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "不欢迎你来这。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DELEGATION_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Expect a delegation bearing exquisite Armenian carpets, and our traditional chili pepper paste, harissa. Should you welcome it, I would be more inclined to stay my hand, or grasp yours."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DELEGATION_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "我们的代表团带着精致的亚美尼亚地毯，以及我们传统的辣酱，哈里萨酱。如果你欢迎我，就跟他们握握手吧，就当是跟我握手。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "If you believe your people can brave the wilds of Armenia, they are welcome to try."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "如果你相信你的人民能够勇敢地进入亚美尼亚的荒野，欢迎他们来尝试。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "You shall not pass."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "你不能过去。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "You are no doubt unsettled by the cavalry bristling at your borders. They wish only to pass."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_OPEN_BORDERS_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "毫无疑问，你对在你的边界逡巡的骑兵感到不安。他们只是想通过。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "We ride together, saddle by saddle."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "让我们一起并排骑马吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Hah! Go eat a horse."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "哈？你胃口太大了。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Friendships are forged in the hunt, strengthened thereafter. Shall we then celebrate ours in the nearest hunting park?"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "友谊可以在打猎中巩固。让我们去附近的围场打个猎吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "String your bow and ready your falcon."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "准备好你的弓箭和猎鹰。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "More's the pity."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_DECLARE_FRIEND_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "非常遗憾。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Consolidate might with guile. A mantra to live by. A mantra we share. Ally with Armenia, and few would dare."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_ALLIANCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "如果我们结成一个同盟，那么诡计和咒语都不能把我们击败，来吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_EXIT_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Your mettle inspires, your ruthlessness commands, and you, leader who saddles the world, have earned my respect."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_KUDO_EXIT_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "你的勇气令人振奋，你的无情令人敬畏，而你，驾驭这个世界的领袖，已经赢得了我的尊敬。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_EXIT_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "The footnotes of history are littered with your kind: milksops remembered only as those trampled underfoot. Right your path, or stand in mine. Either way, history will be made."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_EXIT_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "你这种人只会被扫进历史的角落里，人们只会记得你懦弱的被踩在脚下。让我纠正你的道路，创造历史。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "What an impressive host you've assembled. Truly impressive. But I would rather you not use my borders as a staging ground."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "你组建了一个令人印象深刻的战群。但我希望你不要把我的边界作为一个集结地。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "As we speak, my archers prepare for target practice. Coincidentally, your military loiters uncomfortably close to my borders."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "就在我们说话的时候，我的弓箭手正在准备打靶练习。巧合的是，你的军队在我的边界附近徘徊，令人不安。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_POSITIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "I will leave, but you need not raise your hackles when a friend passes. Instead, consider your borders all the more safer for it."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_POSITIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "我将离开，但不要对我们友善的经过发怒。相反，请考虑你的边界因此更加安全。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_POSITIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "You presume much in warning me. Lucky for you, I am headed elsewhere."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_POSITIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "你很幸运，我正前往其他地方。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_NEGATIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "A force such as mine goes where it pleases."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_TOO_MANY_TROOPS_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_NEGATIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "向我这样的强者想去哪去哪。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "In the best interests of both our civilizations, I ask that you found your next city further afield."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "出于我们文明彼此的利益，我建议你建立城市的时候离远点。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "Continue to settle close to my borders, and I will be forced to expand them."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "如果你继续在我的边境附近定居，我将扩张到这些地方。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_POSITIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "So be it. We will look elsewhere."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_POSITIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "那就这样吧。我们将看看其他地方。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_POSITIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "You need not worry. Had I known your city reeked of tanneries, I would not have settled nearby--downwind or otherwise."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_POSITIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "你不必担心。如果我知道你的城市臭的像在制革，我就不会在附近定居——不管是上风口还是下风口。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_NEGATIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "There is land enough to go around, and resources aplenty. Stay your avarice, for I am a generous neighbor."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_NEGATIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "这里有足够的土地和大量的资源。不必吝啬，因为我是一个慷慨的邻居。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_NEGATIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "Presume to tell me where to settle, and I will found my next city on the ashes of your capital."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_WARNING_DONT_SETTLE_NEAR_ME_AI_RESPONSE_NEGATIVE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "请告诉我你在哪里定居，我将在你们首都的灰烬上建立我的下一个城市。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "Never have I felt so content to be handing over coin."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "我还从来没有对交易感到如此满足过。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "With our business concluded, leave."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_ACCEPT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "我们的交易结束后，请离开。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "You haggle well. Too well for me."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_HAPPY", "你讲价讲得很好。对我来说太好了。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "A miser departs with empty palms, or not at all."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_REJECT_MAKE_DEAL_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_UNHAPPY", "你太过守财，到最后只会两手空空。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Hmph."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "哈。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "If this were the Bacchae, the part of Dionysus would be mine, because you keep finding new ways to anger me. Know you what became of Pentheus? (Denounces You)"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DENOUNCE_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "如果这是《巴克科斯》，狄俄尼索斯的剧情将是对应我的，因为你一直在寻找新的方法来激怒我。你知道彭透斯的下场吗？"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Many have stood before the stone curtain with conquest in their hearts. All have fallen. Make peace with your gods."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "如果你胆敢以征服者的心站在亚美尼亚石城下，你必然会倒下。去跟你的神讲和吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Listen, wretch. Listen and know the thunder beyond your walls is no summer storm, but the hooves of your undoing."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DECLARE_WAR_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "听着，可怜虫。听着，你墙外的雷声不是夏天的暴风雨，而是象征毁灭的马蹄声。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_ACCEPT_DEAL_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "Reconciliation is the aim of all wars. We fight, hoping that when it comes, the terms are ours."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_ACCEPT_DEAL_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "和解是所有战争的结束。我们战斗是希望当它结束时，条约对我们有利。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_REFUSE_DEAL_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "The only hatchet worth burying finds your brow."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_AI_REFUSE_DEAL_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "我的斧头不会同意。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "When you have fought as we have, with indefatigable valor, there is no shame in peace."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_MAKE_PEACE_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "当你像我们一样，以不屈不挠的英勇战斗时，和平就没有什么可耻的了。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "For centuries, Armenia has been hardened in the wars of her neighbors. Now that she has struck out on her own, even my death cannot stop her."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_AI_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "几个世纪以来，亚美尼亚一直在与邻国的战争中淬炼。现在她出击了，即使我死亡也不能阻止她。"),
("en_US", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "For centuries, Armenia has been hardened in the wars of her neighbors. Now that she has struck out on her own, even my death cannot stop her."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_DIPLO_DEFEAT_FROM_HUMAN_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_ANY", "几个世纪以来，亚美尼亚一直在与邻国的战争中淬炼。现在她出击了，即使我死亡也不能阻止她。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_CVS_TIGRANES_II_QUOTE", "Fair kings are seldom remembered for their fairness by those who did not respect their power."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_CVS_TIGRANES_II_QUOTE", "公平的国王很少被那些不尊重其权力的人记住他们的美德。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_CVS_TIGRANES_II_TITLE", "Tigranes II"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_CVS_TIGRANES_II_TITLE", "提格兰二世"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_CVS_TIGRANES_II_SUBTITLE", "Tigranes the Great, King of Armenia"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_CVS_TIGRANES_II_SUBTITLE", "提格兰大帝，亚美尼亚之王"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_CAPSULE_BODY", "Victory for Tigranes is but a process of elimination."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_CAPSULE_BODY", "对提格兰来说，胜利不过是一个成就伟业的过程。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_DETAILED_BODY", "Armenia is the first country ever to adopt Christianity or an organized monothiestic religion. Therefore, Armenia can create a religion as soon as its first Holy Site is completed. This makes Armenia versatile for all victories. Tigranes' military ability and the Arudzi unit gives Armenia an edge in combat. Use all nececary means for the prosperity and development of Armenia. "),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_DETAILED_BODY", "亚美尼亚的使徒教会使得他们是历史上第一个皈依基督教的国家，也是第一个皈依有组织的一神教的国家，因此在游戏中亚美尼亚一旦建造圣地特色区域就可以创立宗教，这使得亚美尼亚的可能性是无穷的。您可以借此获得任何胜利。而提格兰的军事能力和艾路兹枪骑兵也使得亚美尼亚在战争中占有优势。灵活的使用各种手段发展亚美尼亚吧。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "Under King Tigranes II the Great, from 95 to 55 B.C. Armenia thrived, and became the strongest state in the Roman east."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_1", "公元前95年至55年，在提格兰二世大帝的统治下，亚美尼亚蓬勃发展，成为罗马以东最强大的国家。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "In the aftermath of the defeat of Antiochus the Great by the Romans at the Battle of Magnesia in 190 B.C., the grip of the Seleucid Empire on the East was weakened. Armenia was at that time governed by two of Antiochus' generals, Artaxias and Zariadris. Seizing the opportunity, the generals decided to delcare their loyalty to the Roman victors, and claimed autonomy from the ailing Seleucid Empire. For much of its later history, the Kingdom of Armenia would serve as a buffer state between the Roman Empire in the West and the Parthian Empire in the East. Yet, this was not always the case, as Armenia was once a powerful Eastern kingdom during the reign of Tigranes II, also known as Tigranes the Great."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_2", "公元前190年，罗马人在马格尼西亚战役中击败安条克三世后，塞琉古帝国对东地中海的控制力被削弱了。亚美尼亚当时由安条克的两位将军阿尔塔西亚斯和扎里阿德里斯统治。两位将军抓住这个机会，决定放弃对罗马胜利者的忠诚，并要求从衰弱的塞琉古帝国获得自治权。在后来的大部分历史中，亚美尼亚王国将作为西部的罗马帝国和东部的帕提亚帝国之间的一个缓冲国。然而，情况并非总是如此，在提格兰二世（又称提格兰大帝）统治时期，亚美尼亚曾经是一个强大的东方王国。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "Following the independence of Armenia, the satrapy was divided between the two generals. Artaxias ruled over the Kingdom of Armenia, and Zariadris ruled over the Kingdom of Sophene. Tigranes was a descendent of Artaxias, and was born around 140 B.C. Around the age of 20, Tigranes was taken as a hostage by the Parthians, only to be released some 25 years later after ceding 'seventy valleys' in Armenia' to them."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_3", "亚美尼亚独立后，该领土被两位将军瓜分。阿尔塔西亚斯统治着亚美尼亚王国，扎里阿德里斯统治着索菲恩王国。提格兰是阿尔塔西亚斯的后裔，大约出生于公元前140年。大约在20岁时，提格兰被帕提亚人抓为人质，大约25年后，在将“亚美尼亚的70个山谷”割让给他们后，提格兰才被释放。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "Once freed from the Parthians and on the throne of Armenia, Tigranes wasted no time at establishing his position. He first formed an alliance with Mithridates VI of Pontus by marrying his daughter, Cleopatra the Elder. Then, Tigranes set his sights on conquest. At that time, the Kingdom of Sophene was ruled by Artanes, a descendant of Zariadris. Tigranes decided to expand his kingdom, and conquered the lands held by Artanes in 93 B.C. Following the death of Mithridates II of Parthia in 91 B.C., Tigranes successfully reconquered the seventy valleys ceded to him just four years earlier, and laid waste to Parthian lands. Tigranes then conquered Osreoene (Edessa), Nisibis, Gordyene, Atropatene, and Adiabene. He also waged war on the Seleucid Empire, and took Syria and Phoenicia in 83 B.C."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_4", "从帕提亚人手中解放出来并登上亚美尼亚的王位后，提格列斯没有浪费任何时间来确立自己的统治地位。他首先与本都的米特拉达梯六世结成联盟，娶了他的女儿大克利奥帕特拉为妻。然后，提格列斯把目光投向了征服。当时，索菲尼王国的统治者是扎里阿德里斯的后裔阿尔坦斯。公元前91年帕提亚的米特拉达梯二世去世后，提格兰成功地重新征服了四年前割让给他的七十个山谷，并将帕提亚的土地烧毁。随后，提格兰征服了奥斯雷奥尼（埃德萨）、尼西比斯、戈尔迪尼、阿特罗帕蒂尼和阿迪阿比尼。他还向塞琉古帝国发动了战争，并在公元前83年占领了叙利亚和腓尼基。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "Although Tigranes grew rapidly in power, his triumph was to be short-lived. To the west of Armenia, Tigranes' father-in-law, Mithridates VI of Pontus, was at war with the Romans in what is known today as the Third Mithridatic War. Having been defeated by the Roman general Lucullus, Mithridates fled to Tigranes, who refused to hand him over to the Romans. By doing so, Tigranes effectively declared war with Rome."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_5", "虽然提格兰的权力迅速增长，但他的胜利是短暂的。在亚美尼亚以西，本都的米特拉达梯六世，在今天被称为第三次米特拉达梯战争中与罗马人交战。米特拉达梯被罗马将军卢库卢斯打败后，逃到提格兰那里，提格兰拒绝将他交给罗马人。提格兰这样做，实际上是向罗马宣战。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "Although heavily outnumbered by his enemies, Lucullus decided to march on Tigranakert, the new capital of the Armenian Kingdom, in 69 B.C. While the Romans were besieging the city, Tigranes arrived with a huge army, which numbered at 260,000 men. Leaving around 6,000 men to maintain the siege, Lucullus met Tigranes with about 11,000 men. In a surprising turn of events, Tigranes was defeated by Lucullus and was forced to flee to the old Armenian capital, Artaxata, where he was again defeated by the Romans."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_6", "尽管卢库卢斯在人数上大大超过了他的敌人，但他还是决定在公元前69年向亚美尼亚王国的新首都提格拉纳克特进军。当罗马人正在围攻这座城市时，提格兰带着一支人数为26万的庞大军队来到这里。卢库卢斯留下了大约6000人维持围城，并以大约11000人迎战提格兰。在一个令人惊讶的转折中，提格兰被卢库鲁斯击败，被迫逃到亚美尼亚的旧首都阿尔塔萨塔，在那里他又被罗马人打败了。"),
("en_US", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "When the Roman troops grew weary of the eastern campaign, and refused to go any further, Lucullus was recalled by the Senate and replaced by Pompey. In 66 B.C., Pompey marched on Armenia and Tigranes surrendered to the Roman general without a fight. Having reconciled with the Romans, Tigranes became a 'friend and ally' of the Romans with the condition that he give up the territories won through his previous conquests. Tigranes continued to rule over the Kingdom of Armenia until his death in about 55 B.C."),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_PEDIA_LEADERS_PAGE_LEADER_CVS_TIGRANES_II_CHAPTER_HISTORY_PARA_7", "当罗马军队对东部战役感到厌倦，并拒绝进一步行动时，卢库卢斯被元老院召回，由庞培取代。公元前66年，庞培向亚美尼亚进军，提格兰不战而降，向这位罗马将军投降。在与罗马人和解后，提格兰成为罗马人的“朋友和盟友”，条件是他必须放弃之前征服的领土。提格兰继续统治着亚美尼亚王国，直到他在公元前55年左右去世。"),
("en_US", "LOC_UNIT_ARMENIA_APOSTLE_NAME", "Armenia Apostle"),
("zh_Hans_CN", "LOC_UNIT_ARMENIA_APOSTLE_NAME", "亚美尼亚使徒");

